1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/matteo-rosso-orsini_(Federiciana) 
2 CONT -----
2 CONT - [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=lorenfamily&id=I34231&style=TEXT wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com...] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matteo_Rosso_Orsini
2 CONT
2 CONT Matteo Rosso Orsini (1178–1246), called the Great, was Roman politician and father of Pope Nicholas III. He was named a senator of the City of Rome by Pope Gregory IX in 1241: In this capacity he took a firm stand against the vent
2 CONC ures in Italy of Frederick II, Holy Roman Emperor, and defeated him in 1243. He was an effective lord of the Eternal City during sede vacante 1241 and had a considerable influence on the papal election, 1241, when the cardinal ele
2 CONC ctors were confined in Septizonium by his orders. He extended the territories of the Orsini family. He was also a personal friend of St Francis of Assisi and protector of his Order.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letterao/Orsini/orsini.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT    E1. Matteo Rosso “il Grande” (* 1178 + 13-10-1246),
2 CONT
2 CONT Nobile Romano, Signore di Vicovaro, Licenza, Bardella, Cantalupo, Roccagiovine, Galera, Fornello, Castel Sant’Angelo di Tivoli, Nettuno, Civitella, Bomarzo, San Polo e Castelfoglia, Signore di Nerola dal 1235; Signore di Mugnano, 
2 CONC Santangelo e Monterotondo; Senatore di Roma 5-1241/1243.
2 CONT
2 CONT #a)      = ante 1220 Perna, figlia di Giovanni di Crescenzio Caetani (+ 10-12-…..);
2 CONT
2 CONT #b)      = Gemma, figlia ed erede di Oddone Monticelli Signore di Civitella e di Oddolina (+ ante 1232);
2 CONT
2 CONT #c)      = ante 1232 Giovanna dell’Aquila, forse figlia di Ruggero Conte di Fondi (+ 1-1272, sepolta a Roma, sull’Aventino), nipote di San Tommaso d’Aquino (vedi/see)
