2 CONC na and with implicit threat to the Papal State, the unity of the two Aldobrandeschi branches. Yes then began a real war between the Aldobrandeschi (of Sovana and Santafiora) from one side, and Siena and, secondly, Bonifacio VIII a
2 CONC nd Orvieto, on the other. Despite the apparent greater military and political weight of the group controlled by the Pope, the hostilities, after various vicissitudes, they did not end with the full success of the Sienese, because 
