2 CONT  Aldobrandeschi Ildebrandino (XI) il Rosso, + 18.5.1294, # nella chiesa di San Francesco in Orvieto, oo (a) Tommasia o Tommasa NN, oo (b) Francesca di Baschi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conte Palatino, l’11.12.1274 divide il feudo di Soana con i cugini di Santa Fiora ottenendo Pitigliano e Soana, da questo momento appare come 1° Conte di Pitigliano e Soana; fu guelfo fervente e partecipò all’assedio di Montemassi
2 CONC  nel 1260, alle battaglie di Montaperti nel 1260, di Benevento nel 1266 e di Tagliacozzo nel 1268. Sotto le mura del castello di Campagnatico il suo fratello Uberto trovò la morte in circostanze misteriose (1258). ... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=it&u=http://www.wandruszka-genealogie.eu/Antonio/Antonio_Upload/Aldobrandeschi.pdf&prev=search
2 CONT
2 CONT XXII. 4023686 Aldobrandeschi Ildebrandino (XI) the Red, + 18.5.1294, # in the church of San Francesco in Orvieto, oo (a) Tommasia or Tommasa NN , oo (b) Francesca di Baschi. Count Palatine, on 11.12.1274 he divided the fief of Soa
2 CONC na with the cousins ​​of Santa Fiora, obtaining Pitigliano and Soana, from this moment appears as 1st Count of Pitigliano and Soana; it was fervent Guelph and participated in the siege of Montemassi in 1260, to the battles of Mont
2 CONC aperti in 1260, of Benevento in 1266 and of Tagliacozzo in 1268. Under the walls of the castle of Campagnatico his brother Uberto found his death in mysterious circumstances (1258). Ildebrandino the Red took the government of the 
2 CONC County and he moved his seat from Sovana to Pitigliano considering it a safer castle. From there, full of resentment for l & rsquo; killing his brother, he carried out reprisals on the territories he had subjected to Siena. Ildebr
2 CONC andino, unlike his brother, was however more reflective and prudent, so, later, he preferred to use diplomacy to fight against Siena. He he kept the alliance with the Sienese for four years, but then, to defend himself from them, 
2 CONC he stipulated a agreement with Florence, siding with the Guelph party against the Ghibelline party of Siena, e he participated with his troops in the battle of Montaperti, in which he found himself fighting also against his cousin
2 CONC  Conte di Santa Fiora. In the battle the Sienese Ghibellines won i Florentines and the Count of Sovana was taken prisoner and later released after the signature of the peace act. Later, Aldobrandino returned under the protection o
2 CONC f Siena even appointed among the captains of the rsquo; army. From then on he lived a period of peace with the Sienese and consolidated the possessions of the County. Siena, however, continued his work of conquest of the lands of 
2 CONC Maremma, thanks also to alliance agreements with Ildebrandino of Santa Fiora, so Aldobrandino the Red developed closer relations with Orvieto and with the Pope. Meanwhile the troops of Charles of Anjou commanded by Count Guido di 
2 CONC Montfort, came to the aid of the Guelphs and Ildobrandino the Red fought alongside them. The friendship born with Charles of Anjou became closer following the marriage of the one daughter of Ildebrandino, Margherita, with Guido di
2 CONC  Montfort, vicar of the king in Tuscany and cousin of the king of England. ... Meanwhile, the two Aldobrandeschi cousins, the only ones left of the family, they were in constant struggle with each other, until peace was stipulated
2 CONC  in 1274 (nach: http://www.maremmachevai.it von 2016); „In 1274, under the control of Orvieto and Siena, in the presence of David, Bishop of Sovana, Ildebrandino of Count Bonifazio of Santa Fiora and Ildebrandino (Rosso) of Count 
2 CONC Guglielmo di Sovana stipulate a new division of the contado, and also this time the two parts did not have homogeneity of territory and continuity of borders. The county of Santa Fiora began to be more than the Orvieto, ligia ai S
