2 CONT XXIV.1614742 Aldobrandeschi Ildebrandino (VIII), living 1186/1208, testament: Soana 22.10.1208, + ca. 1208 or 1212, oo Adalasia Comitissa (living 1203/1215). Extensive biography of Luciana MARCHETTI in the Biographical Dictionary 
2 CONC of Italians 2 (1960): „Son of Ildebrando (VII) Novello di Sovana, first count palatine, April 27th 1195 had the confirmation from Henry VI of the rights and possessions already guaranteed to his father by Frederick I, with the rec
2 CONC ognition of the qualifications of Count Palatine and of the faithful. This did not prevent him from joining the 4 Dec. 1197 to the Guelph League, established in S. Genesio after the departure of Filippo di Svevia, in order not to 
2 CONC remain isolated among the other forces hostile to the Empire. In 1199, however, it became captain of the people and podestà of Viterbo, who had rebelled against Innocent III, winning the papal troops in Cava di Gorga. He returned 
2 CONC to the Church when in 1202 Siena and Orvieto they allied themselves threatening to encircle it, so as to induce it (1203) to make pacts with the two same cities; between 4 and 21 January with the first, 3 June with the second. It 
2 CONC was a head of the Orvieto cavalry with Ranuccio Farnesi on 20 June 1207 in Montallo della Berardenga, the 31st July following in Montefiascone; acknowledged homage to Innocent III, which confirmed the possession of some castles; p
2 CONC erhaps with the approval of the same Pope in 1209 was following the imperial legate Wolfcherio, patriarch of Aquileia, who took care of restitution by the Municipalities to the empire of what they had taken; subsequently in 1210 a
2 CONC nd 1211, the A. followed by Emperor Otto IV, from whom he had obtained November 1 1209 and 11 Oct. 1210 solemn benefits, including the possession of the lands of Ranieri di Bartolomeo, including also Pitigliano. It is not known ho
2 CONC wever if these last acts are from refer to him or to his son Ildebrandino maggiore, in whose favor and of three other sons, in the 1208, the A. he had made his will. By 1212, however, he had certainly died in that given that Ildeb
2 CONC randino maggiore was confirmed in Orvieto the pacts signed by his father in 1203 
