1 OCCU Countess of Saint-Pol, Brienne, and Conversano, Countess consort of Saint-Pol, and Conversano; AKA "Margaret de Baux" and "Margherita del Balzo", Lady of Andria
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Margaret of Baux==
2 CONT '''Margaret of Baux (French: Marguerite des Baux, Italian: Margherita del Balzo; 1394 – 15 November 1469) was a Countess of Saint-Pol, of Brienne, and of Conversano. She was a member of the noble House of Baux of the Kingdom of Na
2 CONC ples, which had its origins in Provence dating back to the 11th century. Her husband was Peter of Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol, of Brienne, and of Conversano''' (1390 – 31 August 1433). '''Margaret's descendants include''' Engli
2 CONC sh Queen Consort Elizabeth Woodville, King Henry IV of France, Mary, Queen of Scots, and all English monarchs after 1509.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret was born in 1394, the daughter''' of Francis of Baux (1330 – 23 April 1422) by his third wife Sveva Orsini (1360 – c.1430),[1] a descendant of Simon de Montfort, 6th Earl of Leicester and Eleanor of England (daughter o
2 CONC f King John of England).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Her paternal grandparents''' were Bertrand III of Baux, Count of Andria and Squillace, and Marguerite d'Aulnay, and '''her maternal grandparents''' were Nicola Orsini, Count of Nola, Senator of Rome (27 August 1331 – 14 Februar
2 CONC y 1399), and Jeanne de Sabran.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret had two brothers by her father's third marriage to her mother''', Sueva Orsini:
2 CONT
2 CONT William of Baux (Guglielmo del Balzo), Duke of Andria, married Maria Brunforte, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bianchino of Baux (Bianchino del Balzo), was the father of Tesco del Balzo, Governor of Pisa, and chief of the Milanese army. He married Laura Rho, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She had two half-siblings from her father's second marriage''' to Margaret of Taranto:
2 CONT
2 CONT James of Baux (Jacopo del Balzo), Prince of Taranto and Prince of Achaea, Despot of Romania, Lord of Albania and Corfu, Titular Latin Emperor of Constantinople[3] (1353–1384), married Agnes of Naples. The marriage was childless, b
2 CONC ut he had two illegitimate daughters by an unknown mistress.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonia of Baux, Queen consort of Sicily (died 1374), in 1372, married King Frederick III the Simple.[3] The two had no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 8 May 1405, Margaret married Peter of Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol, of Brienne, and of Conversano''' (1390 – 31 August 1433), the eldest son of John of Luxembourg, Lord of Beauvoir and Marguerite of Enghien, Countess of Br
2 CONC ienne and of Conversano, Heiress of Enghien. Peter inherited his mother's fiefs, which included the counties of Brienne and Conversano. He succeeded his aunt Jeanne of Luxembourg, Countess of Saint-Pol and Ligny, as Count of Saint
2 CONC -Pol in 1430. His younger brother John II of Luxembourg, Count of Ligny, an ally of the English during the Hundred Years War, received Joan of Arc as his prisoner, and subsequently sold her to the English, for 10,000 livres.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peter and Margaret had nine children:'''[4]
2 CONT *Louis of Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol, de Brienne, de Ligny, and Conversano, Constable of France (1418 – 19 December 1475), married firstly, in 1435, Jeanne de Bar, Countess of Marle and Soissons (1415 – 14 May 1462), by whom h
2 CONC e had issue, and from whom descended King Henry IV of France and Mary, Queen of Scots. He married secondly, Marie of Savoy (20 March 1448 – 1475), by whom he had further issue. He was beheaded in Paris in 1475 for treason against 
2 CONC King Louis XI.
2 CONT *Jacquetta of Luxembourg (1415/1416 – 30 May 1472), married firstly in 1433, John, Duke of Bedford, and secondly, in secret, c.1436, Richard Woodville, 1st Earl Rivers, by whom she had 16 children,[citation needed] including Eliza
2 CONC beth Woodville, queen consort of King Edward IV of England. Every English monarch after King Henry VII of England descends from Jacquetta's granddaughter, Elizabeth of York, queen consort of England.
2 CONT *Thibaud of Luxembourg, Seigneur de Fiennes, Count of Brienne, Bishop of Le Mans, (died 1 September 1477), married Philippa de Melun, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT *Jacques of Luxembourg, Seigneur de Richebourg (died 1487), married Isabelle de Roubaix, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT *Valeran of Luxembourg, died young.
2 CONT *Jean of Luxembourg, died in Africa.
2 CONT *Catherine of Luxembourg (died 1492), married Arthur III, Duke of Brittany (24 August 1393 – 26 December 1438).
2 CONT *Isabelle of Luxembourg, Countess of Guise (died 1472), married in 1443, Charles, Count of Maine (1414–1472), by whom she had a daughter, Louise (1445–1477), who in turn married Jacques d'Armagnac, Duke of Nemours, by whom she had
2 CONC  six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret died on 15 November 1469 at the age of 75 and was buried in Cercamp Abbey, Frévent, Pas-de-Calais.[5] Her husband Peter had died of plague in 1433.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_Baux
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT *'''Marguerite de Baux1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9
2 CONT *'''F, #16476, b. 1394, d. 15 November 1469
2 CONT *Father	François de Baux, 1st Duke d'Andria, 2nd Comte di Montescaglioso & Squillace2,3,4,6,7,8,9 b. bt 1329 - 1330, d. 1422
2 CONT *Mother	Sueva Orsini2,3,7,8,9 d. a 23 Apr 1422
2 CONT *'''     Marguerite de Baux was born in 1394.3,7,9 She married Sir Pierre of Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Conversano, & Brienne, Seigneur d'Enghien''', son of Sir Jean II de Luxembourg, Count of Conversano & Brienne, Seigneur de 
2 CONC Beauvoir, Richebourg, d'Enghien, & Gouy-sur-Piéton and Marguerite d' Enghien, '''on 8 May 1405; They had 6 sons''' (Louis, Comte de St. Pol, Ligny, Conversano, & Brienne, Constable of France; Philippe, Abbot of Pont St.-Maxente; T
2 CONC hibaut, Seigneur de Fiennes; Jacques, Seigneur de Richebourg & Ruminghem; Valeran; & Jean) '''and 3 daughters''' (Jacquette, wife of John of Lancaster, Duke of Bedford & Anjou, & of Sir Richard Wydeville, 1st Earl of Rivers; Isabe
2 CONC lle/Elizabeth, wife of Charles of Anjou, Duke de Maine; & Catherine, wife of Arthur III, Duke of Brittany, Comte de Richemont & Montfort).2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9 '''Marguerite de Baux died on 15 November 1469; Buried at Abbey of Cercamp, 
2 CONC Artois, France.3,4,5,7,9
2 CONT *'''Family     Sir Pierre of Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Conversano, & Brienne, Seigneur d'Enghien''' b. 1390, d. 31 Aug 1433
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **Theobald (Thibaut) de Luxembourg, Seigneur de Fiennes, Bishop of Le Mans+10,4 d. 1 Sep 1477
2 CONT **Catherine of Luxembourg10 d. 1492
2 CONT **Isabelle de Luxembourg+10,4 d. 1472
2 CONT **Jacques, Seigneur de Richebourg+10 d. 20 Aug 1487
