2 CONT c)         '''PETRUS''' .  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Petrus filius Gregorii Romanorum consulis" and records his donation of the church of St Antonio "in monte Porculo" to Monte Cassino (24 Sep 1077 in the margin), also r
2 CONC eferring to a donation by "superius Gregorius consul Romanorum…cum filio suo Ptolomeo"[846].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Petrus's wife has not yet been identified.  Petrus & his wife had one possible child:
