2 CONT 1.       '''  HUGUES de Baux''' (-[9 Apr 1239/Jul 1240]).  "Raimbaud d'Orange" names "Bertrand de Baux son beau-frère, mari de Tiburge et ses enfants Guillaume, Bertrand et Hugues de Baux…Adhemar de Murvieux et aux enfants qu'il a
2 CONC  eus de sa sœur Tiburgette" in his testament dated 1173[493].  "Hugues de Baux", on the advice of "sa mère Tiburge", granted property to Hugues Pélissier by charter dated 13 Aug 1198[494].  Hugues de Baux swore allegiance to Ymber
2 CONC t d'Aiguières [Archbishop of Arles] for the château de Trinquetaille by charter dated 21 Jan [1191/92][495].  Vicomte de Marseille, de iure uxoris.  "…Guillelmus de Balcio, Hugo de Balcio frater eius…" witnessed the marriage contr
2 CONC act dated 1204 between "Maria filia quondam domini Montispessulani" and "Petro Regi Aragoniæ, et comiti Barchinonis" is dated 1204[496].  A charter dated 17 May 1212 records the division of "des terres et châteaux de la vicomté de
2 CONC  Marseille, hors du territoire de cette ville" between "Roncelin, Giraud-Adhémar et Hugues de Baux, vicomtes de Marseille", Rosselin having, “les châteaux de Saint-Marcel, Roquefort, Jullans, Mazaugues...un deuxième tiers d’Aubagn
2 CONC e”, Girard Adémar "les châteaux de Gardanne, Roquevaire, Gémenos, le Plan d’Aups et [un] tiers d’Aubagne", and Hugues “les châteaux du Castellet, la Cadière, Ceyreste, Seillons, un tiers d’Aubagne”[497].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [Jun 1193/May 1201] ) BARALE de Marseille, daughter of RAYMOND GEOFFROY dit Barral Vicomte de Marseille & his wife Adelaide Porcellet (-before 23 Nov 1234).  "Hugues et Guillaume de Baux" confirmed obligations with respe
2 CONC ct to the port of Marseille with "Geoffroy de Trets, seigneur et Vicomte de Marseille", the latter offering Hugues the possibility of cancelling the obligation after his marriage with Geoffroy's daughter, by charter dated 3 Jan 11
2 CONC 91[498].  "Ildefonse I roi d'Aragon, marquis de Provence" agreed with "Hugues et Guillaume de Baux, frères" to grant half of the town of Marseille to Hugues, as promised as dowry by "Hugues-Geoffroy et Raymond son frère" for his m
2 CONC arriage with the daughter of Hugues-Geoffroy, by charter dated Jun 1193[499].  Vicomtesse de Marseille 1208.  "Hugo de Baucio et domina Barrala eius uxor" confirmed an old convention from "vicecomites Massilie…Ugonem Gaufridi, dic
2 CONC te Barrale avum et Bertrandum fratrem eiusdem Ugonis et Ugonem Gaufridi Sardum nepotem eorum, filium Jaufridi de Massilia" to the bishopric of Marseille by charter dated 15 Apr 1215[500].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Hugues & his wife had four children: 
