2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letteras/SANSEVERINO/SANSEVERINO1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT  F3. (ex 2°) Tommaso (* 1252 ca. + 25-9-1324), 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3° Conte di Marsico, Barone di Sanseverino, Signore di Centola, Polla e Cuccaro dal 1291, Signore di Atena dal 1295, Signore di Postiglione dal 1295 ma rinuncia nel 1298, Signore di Sanza dal 1294, Signore di San Severino di Camer
2 CONC ota, Casal Boni Ripari, Pantuliano, Castelluccio, Cosentino, Corbella, Monteforte (di Vallo), Serre e Padula dal 1301, Signore di Policastro dal 1305, Signore di Tricarico; ebbe la conferma sull’intera baronia del Cilento, Diano, 
2 CONC Lauria, Sant’Angelo a Fasanella e Magliano Vetere, che divise tra i figli; scorta il Duca di Calabria per accogliere il nuovo Re Roberto di Sicilia di ritorno da Avignone (ottobre 1310).
2 CONT
2 CONT a)      = (dote di 1150 once d’oro) ante 1271 Isoarte d’Agoult, figlia di Amiel Signore di Courban e Seaux, Gran Siniscalco di Provenza, e di Alix de Mevouillon (* 1245/1250 + ?);
2 CONT
2 CONT b)      = 1271 Margherita di Vaudémont, figlia di Enrico Conte di Vaudémont, Conte di Ariano e di Margherita de la Roche Signora di Montemiletto
2 CONT
2 CONT c)      = ca. 1285/1290 Sveva d’Avezzano Contessa di Tricarico, figlia ed erede di Grimaldo (Grimaud de Bethzan) Conte di Tricarico e di Elvira della Marra (+ post 1308), vedova di Filippino Polliceno.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#TommasoSanseverinodiedafter1317
2 CONT
2 CONT a)    '''     TOMMASO di Sanseverino''' (-after 1317).  The Istoria of Saba Malaspina names "dominus Thomas comes S. Severini et Marsici" among those who triumphed in the tournament held by Charles I King of Sicily, dated to [1270
2 CONC /71] from the context[170].  The dating of this event suggests that he must have been born from his father´s second marriage, as he was presumably an adolescent or young adult at the time.  Conte di Marsico.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' ([1269/70], contract terminated) to ISOARDE d’Agoult, daughter of AMIEL d’Agoult Seigneur de Curban & his wife --- (-before 1281).  Pollastri records that Charles I King of Sicily [Anjou-Capet] arranged this first 
2 CONC proposed marriage[171].  The bride’s subsequent marriage with Bertrand de Baux confirms that this earlier marriage did not proceed.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly MARGUERITE de Vaudémont, daughter of HENRI [I] Comte de Vaudémont, Conte d’Ariano & his wife Marguerite de la Roche.  Pollastri records a document which confirms this proposed marriage and another which records its
2 CONC  celebration and the birth of her son Enrico[172].  Michel François also refers to the document which records the marriage[173].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ---.  The primary source which names Tommaso’s second wife has not been identified.  The “marenostrum” website names her “ca. 1285/90 Sveva d’Avezzano Contessa di Tricarico, figlia ed erede di Grimaldo (Grimaud de
2 CONC  Bethzan) Conte di Tricarico e di Elvira della Marra (†post 1308), vedova di Filppino Polliceno” [no source cited][174].  The “Bethsan” family is shown in the document JERUSALEM NOBILITY, where “Gremont de Bethsan (-after 1280) is
2 CONC  named as “Signor di Tricario” ("Agrimont de Besan dominus Tricariæ" donated property, held by "Aimerico de Besan patri dicti Agrimont", to the Knights Hospitallers by charter dated 1280[175]) who could have been the right age to 
2 CONC have been Sveva’s father (although “Tricario” appears to have been different from “Tricarico”).  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Tommaso & his first wife had two children: 
2 CONT *i)          ENRICO di Sanseverino . ..
2 CONT *ii)         RUGGIERO di Sanseverino (-[1300/09]).  .. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT   Tommaso & his second wife had two children: 
2 CONT * iii)        GIACOMO di Sanseverino . ..
2 CONT *iv)        GUGLIELMO di Sanseverino .  ..
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -/!\ https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tommaso_II_Sanseverino  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Lists only two wives:  
2 CONT  {and there are 2! The first one is a "Betrothed" / "engagement"!!}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Tommaso II Sanseverino married twice: the first time with Isuarda di Corbano''', daughter of Amelio, who brought him 500 ounces as a dowry and with whom he had Enrico as his only son, while the '''second time with Sveva d'Av
2 CONC ezzano''' , only daughter and heir of Grismondo and last descendant of his family, who, widow of Filippo Polliceno, brought him as a dowry the county of Tricarico with the attached title of count and with whom he had four sons, Ja
2 CONC copo, Guglielmo, Roberto and Ruggero [ 7 ] .
2 CONT
