2 CONT 2.      '''   LEO '''[I] di Gaeta (-[1020/21]).  "Dauferium comitem Triiecti…" and "ex diverso domnum Leonem ducem Fundanum fratrem suprascripti domni Gregorii et domni Dauferii pro vice domnæ Sichelgaitæ uxori suem cum suis conso
2 CONC rtes…domnum Docibilem filium domni Leoni pro vice domnæ Stefaniæ suæ uxoris et pro Gregorio filium domni Docibili secum habendo Docibilem et Gregorium fratres nepoti ipsius domni Gregorii…nos sumus heredes domni Leoni præfecturii"
2 CONC  are named in a charter dated May 992 which settled a boundary dispute between their territories[522].  Duke of Fondi.  "Leo dux Fundane civitatis et filius bone memorie domni Marini…consulis et duci…civitatis Gaetane…et…Sikelgait
2 CONC a ducissa ambo iugalibus" exchanged property with "Jean archiprêtre de la cathédrale de Gaète" by charter dated Oct 995[523].  "Domnum Dauferium comitem Traiectane civitatis" recognised that half of Spinium belonged to Bishop Bern
2 CONC ard by charter dated Apr 999, in the presence of "domnum Marinum et domnum Leonem ducibus Fundane civitatis et domnum Docibilem et domnum Gregorium et domnum Landolfum germanis fratribus filiis domni Gregori ducis"[524].  "Leo…dux
2 CONC  Fundane civitatis" recorded a judgment relating to the inheritance of "bone memorie domnus Iohannes" in favour of "domne Hemilie" by charter dated Feb 1010, in the presence of "Landulfus filius domni Docibili…Landulfus filius dom
2 CONC ni Gregorii duci, Docibili filius domni Leoni magnifici, Gregorius filius domni Leoni magnifici, Leo filio domni Docibili"[525].  "Anna…relicta…domni Docibili bone memorie filii domni Gregorii duci bone memorie" sold one quarter o
2 CONC f her late husband´s property to "domni Iohanni…consuli et duci seniori nostri filio domni Iohanni…consuli et duci bone memorie", in the presence of "domne Hemilie…ducisse senatrix…matri vestre et…domni Leoni…dux Fundane civitatis
2 CONC ", by charter dated Jun 1010[526].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SICHELGAITA, daughter of GREGORIUS & his wife --- (-after Mar 1024).  "Leo dux Fundane civitatis et filius bone memorie domni Marini…consulis et duci…civitatis Gaetane…et…Sikelgaita ducissa ambo iugalibus" exchanged proper
2 CONC ty with "Jean archiprêtre de la cathédrale de Gaète" by charter dated Oct 995[527].  The testament of "Grégoire…fils de feu Léon præfecturus", dated Mar 1024, names "domni Gregorii bone memorie tii nostri et filii domni Iohanni pr
2 CONC efecturii bone recordationis" and "domnus Docibile uterinus frater meus bone memorie…domnus Leone duc Fundane civitatis bone memorie et…domne Sikelgaite ducisse uxori sue" in relation to property of "domni Gregorii bone memorie qu
2 CONC i fuit socero et genitores illorum"[528].  
2 CONT
