1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p3029.htm#i90988
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_II_del_Balzo]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 31 January 1443 Francesco participated in the first General Parliament of the Kingdom of Naples convened by King Alfonso V of Aragon in Benevento , which he had conquered the year before. In 1438 the sovereign appointed him adv
2 CONC isor to the Sacred Royal Council , with an annual commission of 1,000 ducats , and sent him, in the summer of 1451 , as his ambassador, to the court of Emperor Frederick III of Habsburg .
2 CONT
2 CONT The new king Ferrante of Aragon in June 1458 sent Francis to the court of Pope Callixtus III to obtain the investiture of the Kingdom and, after his death, to Pope Pius II to rejoice at the election and pay him homage. In 1459 the
2 CONC  king sent him to represent him on the diet of Mantua which was to prepare the crusade against the Ottomans who had conquered Constantinople .
2 CONT
2 CONT Taking advantage of the distance from the kingdom of the Duke of Andria, the prince of Taranto Giovanni Antonio Orsini del Balzo tried to conquer Andria defended by his son Pirro del Balzo , forcing Francesco to return hastily to 
2 CONC his defense. But, despite the king's intervention, the siege resumed in 1462 with the capitulation of the city and the capture of Francis.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the victorious battle of Troy (1462) against the armies of Duke Giovanni d'Angiò-Valois and the rebellious Neapolitan barons, including the prince of Taranto and the prince of Rossano Marino Marzano , Francesco regained poss
2 CONC ession of the fief of Andria also obtaining the positions of great constable of the Kingdom of Naples and president of the Sacred Royal Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco del Balzo died, according to some with a reputation for holiness, on 8 August 1482 , as the plaque placed on his tomb affirms [1] . His body is kept, mummified, in the Church of San Domenico di Andria. Above the ark is a
2 CONC  bust attributed to Francesco Laurana or, according to others, to Domenico Gagini , who represents him dressed as a tertiary with a collar bearing the Latin motto'''' Ne quid nimis''''  "Do not do too much"  "Don't Overdo it!"
2 CONT
2 CONT FAMILY
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco married on 26 January 1426 with Sancia di Chiaromonte (sister of Isabella , wife of the king of Naples Ferrante d'Aragona), daughter of Tristano , count of Copertino, and of Caterina Orsini del Balzo , who died on 30 Mar
2 CONC ch 1468 and from whom they  had Jacopo, Pirro, Caterina, Antonia, Anghilberto, Duke of Nardò , and Baldassare, Apostolic Protonotary of the Abbey of San Michele Arcangelo of Montescaglioso .
2 CONT
2 CONT WORKS
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco was also a modest man of letters: in 1451 he wrote the Historia inventionis et translationis gloriosi corporis s. Richardi Anglici confessoris et episcopi Andriensis , a hagiographic report relating to the discovery of t
2 CONC he body of San Riccardo di Andria , patron saint of the city, which took place on 23 April 1438 . (The Historia was then published in 1659 in the Italia sacra by F. Ughelli-N. Coleti (vol. 7, Venice, 1721, coll. 1257-62) and in th
2 CONC e Acta Sanctorum (vol. 2, Antverpiæ , 1698, pp. 248 et seq.).
2 CONT
2 CONT HONORS
2 CONT
2 CONT He was made a KNIGHT of tThe Order of the Ermine,    a knightly order established on 29 September 1463 by the king of the Kingdom of Naples Ferrante d'Aragona  . The recipients were given a gold collar with an ermine for pendant, 
2 CONC bearing the Latin motto Malo mori quam foedari ("I would rather die than be dishonored.")   " Amen,"  cousin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See: [https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/francesco-del-balzo_%28Dizionario-Biografico%29/]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#FrancescoBalzoAndriadied1482
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         FRANCESCO (1410-1482 bur Andria Dominicans).  He succeeded his father as Duca di Andria.  Grand Constable of the Kingdom of Naples and Sicily.  Pithon-Curt records his date of death and place of burial (no sources cited
2 CONC )[990].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SANCIE de Clermont [Sancia di Chiaromonte] Contessa di Cuppertino, daughter of BARTHELEMY “Tristan/Tristano” Seigneur de Clermont Conte di Cuppertino & his wife Caterina Orsini del Balzo dei Principi di Taranto, Signora di
2 CONC  Cuppertino.  Pithon-Curt records her parentage and marriage (no sources cited)[991].  Francesco & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
