1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Louis de Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol==
2 CONT '''Louis de Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol, of Brienne, de Ligny, and Conversano (1418 – 19 December 1475) belonged to the Ligny branch of the House of Luxemburg and was Constable of France.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Saint-Pol was the eldest son''' of Peter of Luxembourg and Margaret de Baux. '''His older sister''' Jacqueline, better known as Jacquetta of Luxembourg, married John of Lancaster, 1st Duke of Bedford, and '''Louis was initially
2 CONC  a supporter of the Lancastrian cause in the English Wars of the Roses.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was brought up by his uncle''', John II of Luxembourg, Count of Ligny, '''who named Louis as heir to his estates. However, King Charles VII of France sequestrated the estates''' on John's death in 1441. '''As a result, Saint
2 CONC -Pol sought a rapprochement with the French king and duly had his inheritance restored to him. However, the county of Guise was claimed by Charles, Count of Maine. The affair was settled by an agreement that Saint-Pol's sister Isa
2 CONC belle would marry the Count of Maine and receive the disputed lands as her dowry.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Saint-Pol became a close friend of the Dauphin Louis, the future King Louis XI of France and fought with him in Flanders and in Normandy. However, in 1465 Saint-Pol broke with his friend, now King, to join with the King's broth
2 CONC er, Charles, Duke of Berry in the League of the Public Weal.[1] At the battle of Montlhéry, he commanded the van of Charles the Bold's army, yet later was made constable of France by Louis XI.[1] The Treaty of Conflans ended the w
2 CONC ar, while Saint-Pol received the hand of the King's sister-in-law, Maria of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After this, he was persistently disloyal to the King, conspiring with Charles, Count of Charolais, and with Edward IV of England, his nephew by marriage. The final treason came in 1474 when Saint-Pol approached Charles the Bold
2 CONC , Duke of Burgundy, who had already entered into a compact with Edward IV of England to dismember France in a renewal of the Hundred Years' War. The scheme envisaged the murder of Louis and the sub-division of France between Saint
2 CONC -Pol, the Dukes of Burgundy, Brittany, Bourbon and Namours, the Count of Maine and King Edward. Saint-Pol then proceeded to draw other magnates into the conspiracy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The whole thing started to unravel after Louis and Edward concluded the Treaty of Picquigny in August 1475. Angered by this, Saint-Pol was imprudent enough to write to Edward, upbraiding him as a "cowardly, dishonoured and begg
2 CONC arly king". Edward promptly forwarded the letter to Louis, who now had all the proof he needed. A messenger was sent to the conspirator, in which he was informed that the King had 'need of a head such as his.' He was arrested in S
2 CONC eptember 1475, and later imprisoned in the Bastille. Execution followed in December. Philippe de Commynes, the chief chronicler of Louis' reign, was to write that Saint-Pol had been "abandoned by God because he had tried with all 
2 CONC his might to prolong the hostilities between the King and the Duke of Burgunday."
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1468 to 1472 his chaplain was the well-known translator, author and scribe Jean Miélot.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Louis de Luxembourg married twice, first to Jeanne de Bar, Countess of Marle and Soissons (died 1462), and secondly to Marie of Savoy. He left at least nine legitimate children, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT *John of Luxembourg, Count of Soissons
2 CONT *Pierre II de Luxembourg
2 CONT *Jacqueline of Luxembourg, married Philip I of Croy (died 1511)
2 CONT *Anthony I, Count of Ligny
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_de_Luxembourg,_Count_of_Saint-Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT *'''Louis I de Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Brienne, Conversano, Ligny, & d'Enghien, Governor of Champagne1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *'''M, #19178, b. 1418, d. 19 December 1475
2 CONT *Father	Sir Pierre of Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Conversano, & Brienne, Seigneur d'Enghien3,6 b. 1390, d. 31 Aug 1433
2 CONT *Mother	Marguerite de Baux3,6 b. 1394, d. 15 Nov 1469
2 CONT *'''     Louis I de Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Brienne, Conversano, Ligny, & d'Enghien, Governor of Champagne married Louise Gamegnies DID NOT MARRY.7 Louis I de Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Brienne, Conversano, Ligny, & d'Eng
2 CONC hien, Governor of Champagne Constable of France. He was born in 1418; Age 15 in 1433.3,5 He married Jeanne (Joan) de Bar''', daughter of Sir Robert de Bar, Duke de Bar, Comte de Marle & Soissons, Sire d'Oisy, Grand Butler of Franc
2 CONC e and Jeanne de Bethune, '''on 16 July 1435 at Chateau de Bohain, Bohain-en-Vermandois, Aisne, Picardie, France; They had 5 sons''' (Jean, Comte de Marle & Soissons; Sir Pierre, Comte de St. Pol., Ligny, & Roussy; Charles, Bishop-
2 CONC Duke of Laon; & Philippe) '''and 2 daughters''' (Hélène, wife of Janus of Svoy, Comte de Faucigny; & Jacqueline, wife of Philppe de Croy).2,3,4,5 '''A contract for the marriage of Louis I de Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Brienne, 
2 CONC Conversano, Ligny, & d'Enghien, Governor of Champagne and Marie of Savoy was signed on 1 August 1466; They had 1 son''' (Louis, Prince of Altamura) '''and 1 daughter''' (Jeanne).3,5 '''Louis I de Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Brie
2 CONC nne, Conversano, Ligny, & d'Enghien, Governor of Champagne died on 19 December 1475 at Paris, Seine, Ile-de-France, France; Beheaded.8,2,3,5
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Louise Gamegnies
2 CONT *'''Child	
2 CONT **Jeanne of Luxembourg+9
2 CONT *'''Family 2     Marie of Savoy''' b. 20 Mar 1448, d. 1475
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **Louis II, Prince of Altamura, Duke d'Andria & Venosa, Comte de Ligny d. 31 Dec 1503
2 CONT **Jeanne de Luxembourg, Abbess of Gent10 d. a 1475
2 CONT *'''Family 3     Jeanne (Joan) de Bar''' b. 1415, d. 14 May 1462
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **Jacqueline de Luxembourg+11 d. 1511
2 CONT **Helene de Luxembourg+11 d. 23 Aug 1488
2 CONT **Antoine de Luxembourg, Comte de Brienne, Ligny, & Roussy, Vicomte de Machault, Baron de Rameru & Piney, Seigneur de Pugy, Ghistelles, & Warneton+11 d. 1519
2 CONT **Philippe of Luxembourg10,11
2 CONT **Jean de Luxembourg, Comte de Soissons & Marle, Governor of Burgundy10,11 b. 1437, d. 22 Jun 1476
2 CONT **Peter II de Luxembourg, Comte de Brienne, Roussy, Soissons, Marle, & St. Pol+11 b. c 1440, d. 25 Oct 1482
2 CONT **Charles of Luxembourg, Duke of Luxembourg10,11 b. 1447, d. 24 Nov 1509
2 CONT *Citations
