2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''GREGORIUS''' .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Patricius et consul.  
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Gregorius's wife has not yet been identified.  Gregorius & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         TOLOMEO [I] .  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Petrus filius Gregorii Romanorum consulis" and records his donation of the church of St Antonio "in monte Porculo" to Monte Cassino (24 Sep 1077 in the margin), also r
2 CONC eferring to a donation by "superius Gregorius consul Romanorum…cum filio suo Ptolomeo"[839].  m ---.  The name of Tolomeo's wife has not yet been identified.  Tolomeo & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          TOLOMEO [II] (-25 Feb 1153).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  consul Romanorum.  "Dns Tholomeus" donated property to the church of SS Bonifacius and Alexius by charter da
2 CONC ted 14 Mar 1141[840].  The Annales Ceccanenses record the death "1153 5 Kal Mar" of "Ptolomæus Tusculanus"[841].  m firstly BERTHA, illegitimate daughter of Emperor HEINRICH V & his mistress ---.  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis name
2 CONC s "Bertam filiam suam [=imperator]" wife of "Ptolomeo illustrissimo, Octavia stirpe progenitor, Ptlomei magnificentissimi consulis Romanorum filio" when recording their marriage in 1117 during the Emperor's visit to Rome[842].  m 
2 CONC secondly ---, filia Leonis Petri Leonis.  Tolomeo & his first wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT ***(a)       REGINULFUS [Raino] .  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Reginulfo filio eius [=Tolomeo duce]" recording his father leaving him as a hostage in Rome, in a passage dealing with events in 1137[843]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***(b)       IORDANIS de Gahiniano .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   
2 CONT
2 CONT ***(c)       IONATHAS .  The Annales Pisani record that "Ionatta filius Tolomei de Tusculan" came to Pisa in 1161 and swore allegiance to "Villano archiepiscopo Pisanorum et consulibus"[844].  comes Tusculanus.  He swore fidelity 
2 CONC to the Pope 9 Jul 1155, and in 1170 resigned Tusculum to Pope Alexander III[845]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         GREGORIUS .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *c)         PETRUS .  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Petrus filius Gregorii Romanorum consulis" and records his donation of the church of St Antonio "in monte Porculo" to Monte Cassino (24 Sep 1077 in the margin), also referr
2 CONC ing to a donation by "superius Gregorius consul Romanorum…cum filio suo Ptolomeo"[846].  m ---.  The name of Petrus's wife has not yet been identified.  Petrus & his wife had one possible child:
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          [PETRUS .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  prefect 1116.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT *d)         EGIDIUS .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  m ---.  The name of Egidius's wife has not yet been identified.  Egidius & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          PETRUS .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  diaconus. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **ii)         GUYLLA .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m LANDULF de Santo Iohanne, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *e)         ISDARA .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregory_III,_Count_of_Tusculum
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregory III (died about 1108) was the son of Gregory II. He was the Count of Tusculum from 1058, when his father died. He is usually considered to stand at the fore of the family of the Colonna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unlike his father, he did not bear the ducal and senatorial titles, nor any title to Rome, but simply was patricius et consul, (Comes Tusculanensis, Consul, illustris). Gregory was succeeded by his eldest son, Ptolemy I.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had sons named:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ptolemy I (1099–1129)-(Consul comes Tusculanus);
2 CONT *Gregory IV (1109–1128)-(Iudex Tusculanensis);
2 CONT *Peter de Columpna (1099–1151) - (Colonna family);
2 CONT *Egidius (1128–1137);
2 CONT *Iadara (daughter).
