2 CONT *'''Wikipedia:''' [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludovico_II_Gonzaga,_Marquis_of_Mantua English ] [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludovico_III_Gonzaga Italiano] [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luigi_III._Gonzaga Deutsch]
2 CONT *'''Marquis of Mantua:''' Reign: 1444 -1478
2 CONT >'''Predesessor:'''  [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000003827455161 Gianfrancesco I] '''Successor:'''  [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000006727827834 Federico I]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ludovico Gonzaga, condottiere and court ruler of Mantua, turned his castle named the Corte into a luxurious showplace for the visit of Pope Pius II in 1459. The most impressive room in Gonzaga's Mantua castle was the Sala del Pis
2 CONC anello, a great hall decorated with murals in an Arthurian theme by Pisanello in 1447-48. Mantua was home to a few holy relics, primary among them the "Most Precious Blood" and the lance of Longinus. The blood was supposedly colle
2 CONC cted from the lance which was used to pierce the side of Christ at his crucifixion.
2 CONT Gonzaga initiated a campaign to improve Mantua's appearance after the pope visited his court and reportedly criticized certain aspects of the city. The court architect Leon Batista Alberti advised Ludovico on restoration of Mantua
2 CONC  sites which housed the holy relics. Also foremost in these efforts was Andrea Mantegna who served the Gonzaga for forty-six years as court artist and was knighted by Gonzaga in the 1480s. Mantegna became an accomplished courtier 
2 CONC and so revered was that he dominated the artistic scene of Mantua for many years."
2 CONT [http://www.finearttouch.com/Ludovico_Gonzaga,_The_Court_of_Mantua.html]
2 CONT ---------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ludovico Gonzaga (today known as Ludovico III., but because he was the first Margrave of Mantua with this name he was called "Ludovico or Ludovico I.") , Margrave of Mantua, with his approximately five- or six-year-old grandson G
2 CONC ian Francesco II., the future Margrave of Mantua
2 CONT Born: 5 June 1412
2 CONT Deceased: 12 June 1478
2 CONT Father: Gianfrancesco I. Gonzaga (1395-1444), since 1433 Margrave of Mantua
2 CONT Mother: Paola Malatesta (1393-1449), daughter of Malatesta IV. Malatesta, Signore di Pesaro, and his wife Elisabetta da Varano
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT his brother Carlo Gonzaga, born between 1413 and 1423, deceased in 1456, since 1437 married to Lucia d'Este (1419-1437), daughter of Niccolò III. d'Este
2 CONT his brother Alessandro Gonzaga, born 1415 or 1427, deceased in 1466, married to Agnes da Montefeltro († 1447), daughter of Guidantonio da Montefeltro, Count of Urbino
2 CONT his sister Margherita Gonzaga (1418-1439), since 1435 married to Leonello d'Este (1407-1450)
2 CONT his brother Gianlucido Gonzaga (1421-1448)
2 CONT his sister Cecilia Gonzaga (1425-1451), nun at Santa Chiara in Mantua
2 CONT his sister Leonella Gonzaga, nun
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT Barbara of Brandenburg (1422-1481), first child of Margrave John of Brandenburg and his wife Barbara of Sachsen-Wittenberg; marriage on 12 November 1433
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT his son Federigo, born around 1438 (?), deceased before 1441
2 CONT his daughter Maddalena, born around 1439, deceased as infant
2 CONT his daughter Elisabetta, born around 1440, deceased as infant
2 CONT his son Federigo (I.) (1441-1484), Margrave of Mantua
2 CONT his son Francesco (1444-1483), Cardinal
2 CONT his daughter Paola Bianca (1445-1447)
2 CONT his son Gianfrancesco (1446-1496), Count of Sabbioneta and Lord of Bozzolo; married to Antonia del Balzo
2 CONT his daughter Susanna (1447-1481), nun at Santa Paola in Mantua
2 CONT his daughter Dorotea (1449-1467), married to Galeazzo Maria Sforza, Duke of Milan
2 CONT his daughter Cecilia (1451-1472/78), nun at Santa Chiara in Mantua
2 CONT his son Rodolfo (1452-1495), Lord of Castiglione delle Stiviere, Solferino, Suzzara and Poviglio; first married to Antonia Malatesta, then to Caterina Pico
2 CONT his daughter Barbara (1455-1503), since 1474 married to Eberhard I., Duke of Württemberg
2 CONT his son Lodovico (or Ludovico) (1460-1511), Bishop of Mantua
2 CONT his daughter Paola (1463-1497), married to Leonhard, Count of Gorizia"
2 CONT [https://www.kleio.org/en/history/famtree/vip/638a/]
2 CONT ------------- 
