2 CONT * ...b) '''BEATRIX''' (1161–Château de Vizille, Isère 15 Dec 1228, bur Abbaye de Ayes, near Grenoble). Her parentage and first marriage are confirmed by a chronicle written by "''Guillaume, chanoine de l’église cathédrale de Greno
2 CONC ble''" which records that "''filiam filii sui''" (referring to Marguerite, paternal grandmother of Beatrix) married "''comitem S. Ægidii''"[282]. She succeeded her [father/brother] as Ctss d'Albon. The Chronicle of Alberic de Troi
2 CONC s-Fontaines records the wife of "''Albrico Tailhefer comite Sancti Egidii''" was "''filia senioris Dalfini''" and her second marriage to "''dux''"[283]. The ''Annales S. Benigni Divionensis'' record the marriage of Duke Hugues wit
2 CONC h "''Beatricem, filiam Delfini comitis Alboni apud Sanctum Egidium''"[284]. Her third marriage is confirmed by the following document: “''Hugo Coloniaci''”, leaving for Jerusalem, donated rights in property “''apud Siliniacum''” t
2 CONC o the Chartreuse of Seligna by charter dated 1202, witnessed by “''Beatrix ducissa uxor mea''...”[285]. Valbonnais cites the testament of "''la duchesse Beatrix''" dated 1228 which names "''son héritier le Dauphin André son fils…M
2 CONC atilde sa fille aînée femme de Jean Comte de Chalon…Marguerite son autre fille épouse d’Amédée fils du comte de Savoye''"[286].  
2 CONT * '''m''' firstly (before 11 Oct 1179) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE.htm#Albericdied1183 '''ALBERIC "Taillefer" de Toulouse Comte de Saint-Gilles'''], son of RAYMOND V Comte de Toulouse & his wife Constance de France 
2 CONC (–1183 before 1 Sep). "''Tallifers Viennensium comes et Albonensium comes''" donated property to Oulx by charter dated 11 Oct 1179[287]. "''Taillafers Viennensium et Albonensium comes''" confirmed privileges to the abbey of Durbon
2 CONC , granted by "''pater meus Raymondus dux Narbonæ, comes Tholosæ, marchio Provinciæ''", by charter dated 1183[288]. 
