1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00093367&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bohemond_V_of_Antioch
2 CONT
2 CONT Bohemond V of Antioch (1199−1252) was ruler of the Principality of Antioch, a crusader state, from 1233 to his death. He was simultaneously Count of Tripoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bohemond V was the son of Bohemund IV of Antioch and Plaisance of Gibelet. Like his father before him, Bohemond had a notorious dislike for the Knights Hospitaller and the neighbouring Kingdom of Armenia, preferring an alliance wi
2 CONC th the Knights Templar. Peace with Armenia was assured only shortly before his death, with the mediation of Louis IX of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1225, Bohemond was married to Princess Adela (also known as Alice of Jerusalem), Queen Dowager of Cyprus and Jerusalem, whom he divorced and had the marriage annulled after July 5, 1227, most likely in 1229, without issue. His 
2 CONC second marriage was in 1235 to Luciana (Lucienne) di Segni, a great-niece of Pope Innocent III. He had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Plaisance of Antioch, a daughter who became the third wife of King Henry I of Cyprus in 1251
2 CONT
2 CONT Bohemond VI of Antioch
2 CONT
2 CONT Bohemond V died in January 1252. Since his son and successor was only 15 at the time, he succeeded under the regency of the Dowager Princess, Luciana. However, Luciana never left Tripoli, and instead handed over the government of 
2 CONC the principality to her Roman relatives. This made her unpopular, so the young Bohemond VI gained the approval of King Louis IX of France, who was on Crusade at the time, to get permission from Pope Innocent IV to come of age a fe
2 CONC w months early.
