1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Caracciolo-35
2 CONT
2 CONT This Profile represents the lady known as Teodora, Conti di Chieti sometimes "countess of Teano" or countess of "Teate" (nowdays Chieti, Abruzzo, Italy); the wife of Count Landolfo D'Aquino, Lord of Roccasecca.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT  There is some conjecture regarding the parentage of this lady. 
2 CONT #According to some she was the daughter of Landolfo Caracciolo although she is not mentioned in the lineage of the family on Libro d’Oro della Nobiltà Mediterranea.[2] 
2 CONT #According to other sources she should be Teodora Gallucci, of an other Neapolitan noble family with connections to Teano (Campania, Italy, not far from Aquino). 
2 CONT #In the book of Ferrante della Marra she is mentioned as "Teodora dei conti di Teano, wife of Landolfo d'Aquino. " Memorie Istoriche della Citta di S. Agata dei Goti" confirms that Teodora belonged to the Caracciolo Conti di Chiet
2 CONC i ( than Teate) and not Teano, mentioning also a sister: Albina Caracciolo.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Regardless of her maiden name, she was mother of 12 sons. One of them was San Tommaso d'Aquino one of  leading philosophers of Catholic Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letterad/d'aquino/Aquino-Belcastro.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Landolfo I (+ 24-12- ca. 1245), Lord of Roccasecca, Alvito, Aquino and parts of Monte San Giovanni. Spouse Theodora of the Counts of Chieti (according to others of the Counts of Teano, probably of German or Longobard origin)
2 CONC  (+ shortly after 1250). According to other scholars, it was Teodora Gallucci (see/see) of the accounts of Teano.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * A1. Landolfo II (+ young ante 1257), Lord of Roccasecca, Alvito, Aquino and Monte San Giovanni.
2 CONT * A2. Filippo (+ 1238/1240), Lord of Roccasecca, Giustiziere del Principato. * .........
2 CONT * A3. Jacopo (+ post 25-5-1238), Abbot of San Pietro in Canneto since 1217.
2 CONT * A4. Aimone II (+ post 29-5-1266/ca. 1267), Lord of 1/3 Roccasecca and the barony of Valle di Comino (which  included Gallinara, Picerno, San Donato and Posta), Giustiziere della Sicilia Ultra from 29-5-1266 (dead in office befor
2 CONC e the end of the term of office). ....... of Montenero (?)
2 CONT * A5. Adenolfo I (+ pot 1302), Lord of Roccasecca.  Fiore Foloch (or Fior-of-the other Felluca) Lady of Barbaro and Chestnut in 1276
2 CONT * A6. Rinaldo III (+ post 1238), was referred to as “Magister”, perhaps he had ecclesiastical offices or was a cleric.
2 CONT * A7. '''St. Thomas Aquinas''' “Doctor Angelicus” (* Roccasecca 7-3-1221 or 1224 + Fossanova 7-3-1274), (from 18-7-1323, Doctor of the Church 15-4-1567) Lord of Nusco and Montella but renunciation; ordained priest in 1248, Bacelli
2 CONC ere Biblical of the Dominican General State 1252/1254, Sentencing 1254/1256, Doctor of Theology at the University of the  Paris from 1256 then to Anagni, Orvieto and Salerno, theologian of the Papal Curia from 1259, Master of Theo
2 CONC logy in Paris Since 1264.
2 CONT * A8. Marotta (+ ca. 1257), nun of Santa Maria di Capua since 1245, Abbess from 1252 (confirmed with Papal Bull  of 23-3-1253).
2 CONT * A9. Mary (+ post 1246), Lady of Marano.  Guglielmo Sanseverino 2nd Count of Marsico (see/see)
2 CONT * A10. Adelasia (+ ante 10-5-1305)  Ruggero II dell’Aquila Count of Fondi and Traetto (see/see)
2 CONT * A11. Theodora (+ post 1294/ante 1317)  1246/1256 Ruggero Sanseverino 3rd Earl of Marsico (see/see)
2 CONT * A12. A daughter (+ killed by lightning in Roccasecca in 1226 or 1227).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
