1 NAME Enrico /Sanseverino/ 4°conte di Marsico
2 GIVN Enrico
2 NSFX 4°conte di Marsico
2 _MARNM Sanseverino
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1314
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#TommasoSanseverinodiedafter1317
2 CONT
2 CONT  Tommaso & his first wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)        '''  ENRICO di Sanseverino '''.  He is named in the document cited above under his mother.  A document dated 1309 records a division of the family properties, the “anciens fiefs” [=Marsico] going to Enrico and the “fiefs
2 CONC  nouveaux” to their father’s sons by his second marriage Giacomo and Guglielmo and “ceux qui viendraient à naître”[176]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letteras/SANSEVERINO/SANSEVERINO1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT  G3. (ex 2°)  Enrico (+ 1314),
2 CONT
2 CONT 4° Conte di Marsico (per successione anticipata, Regio Assenso del 12-8-1308), Signore di Cuccaro, Gran Connestabile del Regno di Napoli nel 1313.
2 CONT
2 CONT  = 1305/1310 ca. Ilaria de Lloria Baronessa di Lauria, Signora di Maratea, Ravello, Nicotera e Scalea nel 1325, Signora di Mileto, Signora di Laino e Lagonegro dal 1340, figlia dell’Ammiraglio Ruggero e di Margherita Lanza (testam
2 CONC ento: 1340 ma + 1342/1343) (vedi/see)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''CONNECTED TO THE WRONG MOTHER:'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ -https://it-m-wikipedia-org.translate.goog/wiki/Tommaso_II_Sanseverino?_x_tr_sl=it&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=wapp
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Tommaso II Sanseverino married twice: the first time with Isuarda di Corbano, daughter of Amelio, who brought him 500 ounces as a dowry and with whom he had Enrico''' as his only son, while the second time with Sveva d'Avezza
2 CONC no , only daughter and heir of Grismondo and last descendant of his family, who, widow of Filippo Polliceno, brought him as a dowry the county of Tricarico with the attached title of count and with whom he had four sons, Jacopo, G
2 CONC uglielmo, Roberto and Ruggero [ 7 ] .
2 CONT
2 CONT
