2 CONT ii)         RICCARDO (-[after 1154]).  "Richard frère de Geoffroy d´Aquila" is named in a charter dated May 1132[447].  [The Ignoti Monachi Chronica records that in the first year of the reign of Guillaume I King of Sicily, [1154/
2 CONC 55], "Robertus, qui fuerat princeps Capuanus, Robertus comes de Lauritello consanguineus regis et comes Andreas nepos condam Raynulfi" by whom he had "filium Symonem, quem constituit principem Capue" invaded the kingdom "cum Greco
2 CONC rum exercitu" and subjugated "totam Apuliam et Terram Laboris", and that "Robertus" was captured "in flumine Gariliano a comite Riccardo de Aquila" and sent to the king as a prisoner[448].  It is not known whether the latter refer
2 CONC ence is to Riccardo, to his son of the same name or to his nephew Riccardo son of Goffredo.]  m ---.  The name of Riccardo´s wife is not known.  Riccardo & his wife had one child: 
