2 CONT *''''''Margaret WOODVILLE (C. Arundel)
2 CONT *''''''Born: ABT 1439
2 CONT *''''''Died: BEF 6 Mar 1490/1
2 CONT *''''''Buried: 16 Mar 1490/1, Arundel, Sussex, England
2 CONT *Father: Richard WOODVILLE (1° E. Rivers)
2 CONT *Mother: Jacquetta Zu St. POL of Luxembourg (D. Bedford)
2 CONT *''''''Married: Thomas FITZALAN (16° E. Arundel)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. William FITZALAN (17° E. Arundel)
2 CONT **2. Margaret FITZALAN (C. Lincoln)
2 CONT **3. Edward  FITZALAN
2 CONT **4. Joan FITZALAN (B. Abergavenny)
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/WOODVILLE.htm#Margaret WOODVILLE (C. Arundel)
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *''''''Margaret Woodville1 
2 CONT *''''''F, #107491, b. circa 1439, d. before 6 March 1490/91
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 May 2004
2 CONT *''''''     Margaret Woodville was born circa 1439.1 She was the daughter of Sir Richard Wydevill, 1st Earl Rivers and Jacquetta de Luxembourg.1 She married Sir Thomas FitzAlan, 17th Earl of Arundel, son of Sir William Fitzalan, 1
2 CONC 6th Earl of Arundel and Joan Neville.1 She died before 6 March 1490/91.1 She was buried at Arundel Castle, Arundel, Sussex, England.2
2 CONT *''''''     Margaret Woodville was also known as Margaret Widville.2
2 CONT *''''''Children of Margaret Woodville and Sir Thomas FitzAlan, 17th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT **Sir William FitzAlan, 18th Earl of Arundel+ b. c 1476, d. 23 Jan 1543/442
2 CONT **Joan FitzAlan+ b. b 1484, d. 14 Nov3
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 124. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct
2 CONC  or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 250. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 33.
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p10750.htm#i107491
