1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Charles, Count of Maine==
2 CONT '''Charles du Maine (Château de Montils-lez-Tours, 1414 – 1472, Neufvy-en-Touraine) was the third son''' of Louis II of Anjou and Yolande of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1434, he married Cobella Ruffo (d. 1442), Countess of Montalto and Corigliano, he had one son:
2 CONT *Jean Louis Marin, died as an infant
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1437, he took up arms on behalf of Charles VII of France, participating in the capture of Montereau, and that of Pontoise in 1441. At this time, his brother René ceded to him the County of Maine. He continued to take part in
2 CONC  Charles' campaigns.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By his second marriage in 1443 to Isabelle of Saint-Pol''' (d. 1472), daughter of Peter of Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol, '''he had two children:
2 CONT *Louise (1445–1477, Carlat), married 1462 at Poitiers Jacques d'Armagnac, Duke of Nemours (d. 1477)
2 CONT *Charles IV, Duke of Anjou (1446–1481)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A dispute over the county of Guise between Charles and Isabelle's brother''' Louis de Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol '''was settled by settling it upon Isabelle as a dowry.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He led the rearguard for King Louis XI at the Battle of Montlhéry.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles,_Count_of_Maine
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT *'''Charles d' Anjou, Duke du Maine, Comte de Guise & Gien1,2,3
2 CONT *'''M, #48454, b. 14 October 1414, d. 10 April 1472
2 CONT *Father	Louis II, King of Naples, Sicily, & Jerusalem, Duke of Anjou1 b. 5 Oct 1377, d. 26 Apr 1417
2 CONT *Mother	Jolanta of Aragon1 b. 1384, d. 14 Dec 1443
2 CONT *'''     Charles d' Anjou, Duke du Maine, Comte de Guise & Gien was born on 14 October 1414 at Chateau Montils-lez-Tours, France.1 He married Cobella Ruffo''', daughter of Carlo Ruffo, 2nd Count Montalto & Corigliano, Signore di P
2 CONC aola, Acerenza, & Fuscaldo and Ceccarella Sanseverino, '''in 1434.4 Charles d' Anjou, Duke du Maine, Comte de Guise & Gien Vicomte de Chatellerault, de Matigne, Seigneur de la Ferte-Bernard. in 1435.1 He married Isabelle de Luxemb
2 CONC ourg''', daughter of Sir Pierre of Luxembourg, Count of St. Pol, Conversano, & Brienne, Seigneur d'Enghien and Marguerite de Baux, '''on 9 January 1443.5,2 Charles d' Anjou, Duke du Maine, Comte de Guise & Gien died on 10 April 14
2 CONC 72 at Neufvy-en-Touraine, France, at age 57; Buried at Le Mans Cathedral.1,2
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Cobella Ruffo''' d. 1442
2 CONT *'''Child	
2 CONT **Charles IV d' Anjou, Duke of Maine & Anjou, Comte de Guise & Provence, King of Sicily & Jerusalem4 b. 1436, d. 11 Nov 1481
2 CONT *'''Family 2
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **Louis d' Anjou, Baron de Mezieres en Touraine, Ste. Neomaye, Pree, & Seneche+6
2 CONT **Marie of Anjou7,3 b. c 1437, d. a 1471
2 CONT *'''Family 3     Isabelle de Luxembourg''' d. 1472
