1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/ezzelino-ii-da-romano_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ezzelino_II_da_Romano Si sposò quattro volte: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Agnese''' di Azzo V d'Este, da cui ebbe Palma, andata in sposa nel 1207 a Gualpertino da Cavaso.
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Speronella''' di Dalesmanino Dalesmanini, dalla quale non ebbe figli.
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Cecilia''' d'Abano, che gli diede Agnese.
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Adelaide''' dei conti di Mangona, da cui gli nacquero le figlie Palma Novella, Emilia (sposata ad Alberto dei conti di Vicenza), Sofia e Cunizza, e i figli Ezzelino III e Alberico.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%201100-1400.htm#EzzelinoIIRomanodied1235
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         EZZELINO [IV] "il Monaco" da Romano ([1150]-1235).  The Cronica Alberti de Bezanis names "fillius primi Ezelini…primo filliam unicam Cunizam" and "secundo fillium Ezzelinum" as the children of "dominus Ezelinus de Roman
2 CONC o qui dictus est Balbus"[1192].  Podestà di Treviso.  A charter dated 27 Jun 1191 records wrongs done by "dñi Eccelini de Romano Tar. Potestatis" to the church of Treviso[1193].  A charter dated 2 Mar 1192 records a judgment issue
2 CONC d by "Ecelino de Romano Tarvisii Potestas"[1194].  "Dñus Ezelinus de Romano filius q. Dñi Ezelini" sold property "in Angarano" to the monastery of Campesion by charter dated 20 Sep 1202[1195].  The Book of Statutes of Treviso date
2 CONC d 1207 names "Rodulfo comitis Widonis Borgognonis filio civitatis Tarvisii potestati" and "Ecelini de Romano…"[1196].  "Dño Ugulino, Bartholomeo, Vendramino fratribus de Cesana et Roberto eorum nepote simul consortibus comitatus C
2 CONC esane" sold "comitatus Cesane…unam medietatem" to "dñi Ezzelini" by charter dated 28 Mar 1218[1197].  A charter dated 21 Jun 1218 records the peace agreement between the city of Vicenza and "Dñus Ecelinus de Romano", agreed by "Ic
2 CONC ilinellus filius dñi Ecelini"[1198].  "Dñus Ecelinus de Romano" divided his property between "Ecelini et Alberici filiorum eius" by charter dated 5 Jul 1223[1199].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly as her first husband, AGNESE d'Este, daughter of AZZO [V] d'Este & his wife ---.  The Cronica Alberti de Bezanis states that "Ezelino secundo" had two wives in his boyhood, firstly "dominam Agnetam sororem domini A
2 CONC zonis primi marchionis Estensis" who after her divorce married "domino Dulcemanino…de Padua"[1200].  She married secondly Dulcemanino di Padua.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ALEIDA di Mangono, daughter of ---.  The Cronica Alberti de Bezanis states that "Ezelino secundo" had two wives in his boyhood, the second of whom was "Aledeytam sororem comitum de Mangono qui etiam comites Rabios
2 CONC i nominantur"[1201].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1):  MARIA di Campreto, daughter of ---.  The Cronica Alberti de Bezanis names "dominam Aledaxiam" as illegitimate child of "Ezelino secundo" and his "amorum illicitum dominam Mariam de Campreto, consanguineam illo
2 CONC rum de Campo Sancti Petri set ex altera parentella"[1202].
2 CONT
2 CONT    Ezzelino [II] & his first wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         CECILIA .   ...
2 CONT **i)          ASEDISIO .   ...
2 CONT
2 CONT   Ezzelino [II] & his second wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         PALMA Novella (-before 4 May 1218). ... ... ...
2 CONT *c)         IUNIA [Imia/Emilia] . ... ...
2 CONT *d)         SOPHIA . ...
2 CONT *e)         EZZELINO [V] da Romano (6 Apr 1194-in jail Sarcino 27 Sep 1259, bur Castro Sulcini). ... .... .... .... ....
2 CONT *f)          ALBERIGO da Romano (-killed San Zeno 1260). ... .... .... .... ....
2 CONT *g)         CUNIZA (-after 1 Apr 1265). ... ... .... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT   Ezzelino [II] had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *h)         ALEDAXIA .   
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
