2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ptolemy II''' (also ''Ptolemæus'' or ''Tolomeo'') (died 1153) was the count of Tusculum and consul of the Romans (consul Romanorum) from 1126 to his death. He was the son and successor of Ptolemy I. .. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letterac/Colonna/COLONNAANTICO.htm<br/>
2 CONT B1. Tolomeo II (+ post 1153), Conte di Tuscolo, Prefetto di Roma nel 1116.
2 CONT
2 CONT  /!\             = Berta Pierleoni, di nobile casata romana
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20ITALY.htm#_ftnref839<br/>
2 CONT i)          '''TOLOMEO''' [II] (-25 Feb 1153).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  consul Romanorum.  "Dns Tholomeus" donated property to the church of SS Bonifacius and Alexius by charte
2 CONC r dated 14 Mar 1141[840].  The Annales Ceccanenses record the death "1153 5 Kal Mar" of "Ptolomæus Tusculanus"[841].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly BERTHA, illegitimate daughter of Emperor HEINRICH V & his mistress ---.  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Bertam filiam suam [=imperator]" wife of "Ptolomeo illustrissimo, Octavia stirpe progenitor, Ptlomei magn
2 CONC ificentissimi consulis Romanorum filio" when recording their marriage in 1117 during the Emperor's visit to Rome[842].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ---, filia Leonis Petri Leonis.  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Tolomeo & his first wife had three children:
2 CONT *(a)       REGINULFUS [Raino] .  The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Reginulfo filio eius [=Tolomeo duce]" recording his father leaving him as a hostage in Rome, in a passage dealing with events in 1137[843]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(b)       IORDANIS de Gahiniano .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   
2 CONT
2 CONT *(c)       IONATHAS .  The Annales Pisani record that "Ionatta filius Tolomei de Tusculan" came to Pisa in 1161 and swore allegiance to "Villano archiepiscopo Pisanorum et consulibus"[844].  comes Tusculanus.  He swore fidelity to
2 CONC  the Pope 9 Jul 1155, and in 1170 resigned Tusculum to Pope Alexander III[845]. 
