2 CONT 8.         ALASIE ([1185/93?]-after Mar 1249, bur abbaye de Bonnevaux).  Her birth date is estimated based on the rather tight chronology for her two marriages.  The testament of “Flote [dame de Royans]”, dated Dec 1231, appointed
2 CONC  “sa mère Alays” as universal heir, naming “Adhemarius de Poitiers son fils, qu’elle avait eu de Guillaume de Poitiers son mari” as substitute[2173].  Under her testament dated Mar 1249, "Alays de Roians, domina castri Sancti Joha
2 CONC nnis de Bornay, uxor quondam nobilis viri dom Ose Sicce" elected burial "apud…monasterium Bone Vallis", donated property for the anniversary of “nobilis viri quondam domi Drodoni de Bello Visu primi mariti mei”, bequeathed propert
2 CONC y to "Dome Sibille uxori nobilis viri domi Audemari de Pictavia, nepotis mei…nobilem domam Flotam filiam meam…Ugone nepoti meo de Turre, senescalco Lugdunensi" and also names "fratre meo dome Alberto de Turre"[2174].  m firstly DR
2 CONC ODON de Beauvoir, son of --- (-[1205/07?]).  m secondly ([1207/09?]) RAIMBAUD Bérenger de Royans "Ossassica" Seigneur de Royans, son of GUIDELIN & his wife --- ([before 1185?]-before Feb 1234). 
