1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT PROVENCE - VALENTINOIS, DIOIS 
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 16 July 2025
2 CONT Chapter 6
2 CONT D.      SEIGNEURS de MONTEIL, de MONTELIMAR, de PEYRINS (ADEMAR/ADHEMAR)
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provvaldi.htm#_Toc97476366
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT HUGUES [de Valence, son of '''ADEMAR Comte de Valence & his wife Rotilde -'''--] .  "Ademarus comes [Valentinensis] [et] Roteldis uxor mea" confirmed the donations to Cluny by his father by charter dated 1037 jointly with "filii n
2 CONC ostri Pontio episcopo, Ugone, Lamberto, Gontardo, Geraldo"[882].  Chevalier proposes that Hugues, father of the brothers Guillaume, Adémar and Lambert, all named in the Cluny charter dated to [1049/1108] quoted below, was the same
2 CONC  person as Hugues son of Adémar Comte de Valence[883]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maison_d%27Adhémar
2 CONT
2 CONT The house of Adhémar was an illustrious and ancient family of the nobility of Dauphiné. She was in the Middle Ages one of the most powerful in her province. Old and controversial genealogies have given him without proof of fancifu
2 CONC l origins and homonymous families have claimed to be attached to it.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Joseph Cyprien Nadal, the filiation of the Adhémar house can only be attested from the first Baron of Grignan: Hugues Adhémar, Lord of Monteil and Viscount of Marseille. Between 1032 and 1045, after a youth devoted to
2 CONC  the career of arms, he married Marthe of Toulouse and settled in his barony of Grignan. He will have, among others, five boys[5]:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Giraud I, the eldest, who died in 1095, will be the second Baron of Grignan from 1077.
2 CONT # Adhémar, after a beginning of his military career, will be canon of Valence and then bishop of Le Puy in 1087; during the Council of Clermont, he will preach alongside Pope Urban II the first crusade[6] in which he will particip
2 CONC ate as an apostolic legate with his brother William and his four nephews, son of Giraud I: Lambert (third baron of Grignan) died in 1099 under the walls of Jerusalem, Giraud II (fourth baron of Grignan), Giraudet at the origin of 
2 CONC the cadet branch of the lords of La Garde, and Giraudonnet also died in 1099 under the walls of Jerusalem, after his uncle Adhémar Victim of the plague on August 1, 1098 in Antioquia.
2 CONT # Left-handed, monk, then abbot of Notre-Dame-d'Aiguebelle-de-Montjoyer, first of the name. Indeed, this first abbey of Notre Dame d'Aiguebelle was founded in 1045 by the first Baron of Grignan, Hugues Adhémar, for his son Gaucher
2 CONC , with the consent and on the land of his neighbor the Lord of Rochefort, in the forest of Montjoyer. It was consecrated on March 25, 1045 by Odalric III, bishop of Saint-Paul-Trois-Châteaux[7]. Subjected to the warlike vicissitud
2 CONC es of the time, it was abandoned in 1137 and refounded not far from there on the land of Réauville by Gontard Loup, Lord of Rochefort[8]. It still remains today in the same place, but depends administratively on the municipality o
2 CONC f Montjoyer, this village having been built since then on the site of the first abbey.
2 CONT # Guillaume-Hugues, monk in La Garde at the convent of Notre-Dame-du-Val-des-Nymphes, of which he will become the prior, died in front of Jerusalem in 1099 shortly after his two nephews Lambert and Giraudonnet died on Good Friday.
2 CONT # Hugues, husband of Agathe de Foix, will receive the city of Lombers as an apanage and will be at the origin of the Languedoc branch of the Adhémar lords of Lombers-en-Albigeois extinct in the fourteenth century[9].
