2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provvaldi.htm#RaymondIIBauxOrangeCourthezondied1279B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''RAYMOND [II] de Baux''', son of GUILLAUME [II] de Baux co-Prince d’Orange & his wife Précieuse --- (-before 29 Oct 1279).  The testament of "Guillaume de Baux III co-prince d’Orange fils de feu Guillaume II prince et de dame Pr
2 CONC écieuse", dated 1 Jun 1248, named as successive substitutes “Bertrand son frère” (on condition that he left the church and married) and “Raymond de Baux I son oncle prince d’Orange” (on condition of leaving “en faveur de Bertrand,
2 CONC  de la jouissance des revenues de Courtheson” and property to “Raymond de Baux son frère”)[689].  Co-Prince d’Orange.  A charter dated 2 Feb 1265 records an agreement between "Raymond de Baux I, Raymond II son neveu, seigneur de S
2 CONC uze, prince et co-prince d’Orange" and “Roncelin de Fos maître de l’ordre du Temple en Provence” regarding property bequeathed to the Templars “par Guillaume III co-prince d’Orange, qui, au mépris de son testament de 1248, et en h
2 CONC aine de son oncle et de son frère”[690].  Seigneur de Suze et de Solérieux: "Raimundus de Baucio juvenis Princeps Arausicæ et dominus Castri de Suza, ac major dominus Castri de Solorino“ acknowledged allegiance to the Bishop of Sa
2 CONC int-Paul-Trois-Châteaux by charter dated 10 May 1272, with the consent of “Pontii de Monte-dracone Domini de Cantamerulis et Domini de Solorino” and witnessed by “Domino Raimundo de Baucio Principe Arausicæ avunculo dicti nobilis 
2 CONC Raimundi de Baucio...”, the bishop raising his standard at Suze 15 May 1272 in the presence of “dicti nobilis Raimundi de Baucio domini dicti castri de Suza et Bertrandi de Baucio eius filii et nobilis Lauræ eius uxoris” who ratif
2 CONC ied the earlier charter[691].  The 29 Oct 1279 of his son Bertrand [III], quoted below, records that his father was deceased at the time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There is some doubt about Raymond’s marriage(s). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[m''' firstly BIGNE, daughter of ---.  She is named in the following document: "Bertrand de Baux IV fils de Raymond I et de dame Malberjone pour trois parts" and [her son] “Bertrand de Baux III fils de Raymond de Baux II et de 
2 CONC dame Bigne pour une part” confirmed the names of officials in Orange by charter dated 6 Dec 1282[692].  Pithon-Curt, after naming “Laure Adhémar...fille d’Aimar Baron de Grignan Coseigneur de Monteil et de Clémence” as the wife of
2 CONC  Raymond [II], notes that “N--- Le Sieur de la Pize” named her “Bigne” (presumably based on this 6 Dec 1282 charter) (and also that “le Sçavant Peirest, Ermengarde”, no citation reference), adding “peut-être eut-il deux femmes?”[6
2 CONC 93].  The name “Bigne” has not been traced elsewhere and could presumably be a nickname.  If that is correct, “Bigne” may have been the same person as Laure Adhémar: Bert M. Kamp has also highlighted the onomastic connections betw
2 CONC een the Adhémar family and Raymond [II]’s descendants, for example the use of the names Rixende (one of Laure’s paternal aunts[694]) for his daughter and Mabile (Laure’s sister) for his granddaughter, which suggest that this possi
2 CONC bility may be correct[695].''']''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [secondly?] LAURE Adhémar, daughter of ADEMAR Adémar de Monteil & his wife ---.  "Raimundus de Baucio juvenis Princeps Arausicæ et dominus Castri de Suza, ac major dominus Castri de Solorino“ acknowledged allegiance to the
2 CONC  Bishop of Saint-Paul-Trois-Châteaux by charter dated 10 May 1272, the bishop raising his standard at Suze 15 May 1272 in the presence of “dicti nobilis Raimundi de Baucio domini dicti castri de Suza et Bertrandi de Baucio eius fi
2 CONC lii et nobilis Lauræ eius uxoris” who ratified the earlier charter[696].  Pithon-Curt records “Laure Adhémar...fille d’Aimar Baron de Grignan Coseigneur de Monteil et de Clémence” as the wife of Raymond [II] (no source cited apart
2 CONC  from the 10/15 May 1272 charter)[697].  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Raymond [II] & his [first/second] wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
