1 NAME Bertrand /des Baux/ Comte d'Avellino
2 GIVN Bertrand
2 NSFX Comte d'Avellino
2 _MARNM des Baux
1 NAME Bertrand des Baux, I. conte di Avellino
1 SEX M
1 OCCU unknown
2 PLAC comte d'Avelin
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1268
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1312
1 OCCU Comte d'Avellino
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#BertrandAvellinodied1304
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BERTRAND de Baux''', son of BARRAL Seigneur de Baux & his wife Sibylle d'Anduze (-[21 May/22 Jul] 1304).  Alphonse Comte de Poitou et de Toulouse "senescallo Venaissini" wrote to "Barralli domini Baucii et Bertrandi eius filii,
2 CONC  militum" concerning a dispute "inter homines de Montiliis {Monteux, Vaucluse, cant. Carpentras} et de Auriolo {Loriol, Vaucluse, cant. Carpentras} ex una parte et homines de Sarriano {Sarrians, Vaucluse, cant. Carpentras} ex alte
2 CONC ra", dated 31 Jul 1267[429].  He fought at the battle of Benevento against Manfred King of Sicily and was appointed Conte di Avellino by Charles I King of Sicily [Anjou-Capet][430].  "Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin, fils de Barr
2 CONC al seigneur des Baux" acknowledged holding “le château de Trinquetaille” in fief from the archbishop of Arles by charter dated 25 Jun 1275[431].  "Bertrand de Baux III co-prince d’Orange et Raymond son frère, fils et héritiers de 
2 CONC Raymond II seigneur de Suze et co-prince d’Orange", in the presence of “leur oncle Raymond de Baux I”, granted their rights “sur la terre de Bardineto, province de Gênes, et même dans le judicat de Torres, Arborée, Gallura et au c
2 CONC hâteau de Bosa” to “leur cousin Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin” by charter dated 3 Oct 1280[432].  Seigneur de Pertuis: "Guillaume de Pertuis fils de feu Guillaume de Sabran comte de Forcalquier" transferred the usufruct of prop
2 CONC erty of "son fils Bertrand de Baux" to “Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin”, referring particularly to the dowry of “feue Alasacie de Baux son épouse tante du comte d’Avellin et mère de feu Bertrand de Baux de Pertuis”, by charter d
2 CONC ated 6 Oct 1284[433].  "Bertrand de Baux...seigneur de Baux, comte d’Avellin" sold rights in Arles and Trinquetaille to the archbishop of Aix, promising that "Agathe son épouse" would ratify the agreement, by charter dated 25 Sep 
2 CONC 1300[434].  A charter dated 1303 records that "Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin", due to financial difficulties, granted “tout ce qu’il tient de l’église de Marseille” to “son fils Raymond” provided he gave dowries “à ses deux fil
2 CONC les et de nourrir les deux fils qu’il a de son second mariage”[435].  A charter dated 21 May 1304 records a complaint brought by "les habitants di château de Goult...par devant Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin leur seigneur suzera
2 CONC in"[436].  He presumably died before 22 Jul 1304, the date of the charter quoted below in which his son Raymond is named as Conte di Avellino. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (before 12 Oct 1254) PHILIPPA de Poitiers-Valentinois, daughter of AYMAR [III] de Poitiers Comte de Valentinois et de Diois & his first wife Sibylle de Beaujeu (-before 27 Apr 1283).  By charter dated 10 Apr 1244, 
2 CONC "Aymar de Poitiers III comte de Valentinois, fils de feu Guillaume et de Florie" confirmed his desire for the marriage of "sa fille Philippine" to "Hugues fils ainé de Barral seigneur de Baux", when they reached the age of puberty
2 CONC , or if he died to "Bertrand fils cadet de Barral"[437].  Considering the chronology of the family, Philippa must have been a baby at the time and was probably her parents' first child.  Her marriage took place before the charter 
2 CONC dated 12 Oct 1254 under which "Philippine fille d'Aymar de Poitiers comte du Valentinois, épouse de Bertrand de Baux d'Avellin" confirmed the payment of her dowry by her father[438].  The testament of "Aimarus de Pictavia Comes Va
2 CONC lentinensis filius quondam domini Guillelmi de Pictavia comitis Valent.", dated 20 Apr and 6 May 1277, leaves bequests to "…Philippam filiam suam uxorem domini Bertrandi domini de Baucio…Margaritam filiam suam uxorem Rotgerii de C
2 CONC lairiaco…Guillelmetum filium suum quem habuit ex ipsa domina Alixente"[439]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (before 26 Nov 1283) as her second husband, AGATHE de Mévouillon, widow of SICARD [III] Aleman, daughter of RAYMOND de Mévouillon & his wife Beatrix [Comtesson] [de Genève] (-after 16 Nov 1313).  "Béatrix de Mévou
2 CONC illon dame de Visan, veuve de Sicard Aleman le vieux" and “Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin en sa qualité de mari d’Agathe de Mévouillon sœur de Béatrix” acknowledged receiving the sale price “du château de Saint-Sulpice” by chart
2 CONC er dated 26 Nov 1283[440].  "Bertrand de Baux...seigneur de Baux, comte d’Avellin" sold rights in Arles and Trinquetaille to the archbishop of Aix, promising that "Agathe son épouse" would ratify the agreement (which she died by c
2 CONC harter dated 8 Oct 1300), by charter dated 25 Sep 1300[441].  Dame de Caromb: "Agathe veuve de Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin" ordered “la communauté d’Aulan” to pay “les décimes au prieur de Notre-Dame de Mévouillon”, dated at 
2 CONC Caromb 25 Sep 1305, 19 Dec 1306, 4 Oct 1307, and 24 Nov 1307[442].  "Agathe de Baux dame de Caromb veuve de Bertrand de Baux comte d’Avellin et Agout de Baux son fils" donated “aux cardinaux du Comtat” their rights “dans le territ
2 CONC oire de Caromb sur la fontaine...Fons d’Alps” by charter dated 16 Nov 1313[443]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Bertrand & his first wife had two children:
2 CONT  Bertrand & his second wife had five children:
