1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillaume_III_Roger_de_Beaufort
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.    '''     GUILLAUME [III] Rogier de Beaufort'''  ([1320/30]-28 Mar 1394).  A manuscript genealogy of the Beaufort family (date not specified) records that “Guillelmus Rogier alias de Belfort” and his first wife “Guerinam de Ca
2 CONC nilliaco” had four sons “Guillelmum comitem Bellifortis et vicecomitem Turenæ, Petrum Papam Gregorium XI Rogerium, et Nicolaum et Marquesiam”[1656].  Vicomte de Turenne.  His sister-in-law Cécile de Comminges sold the viscounty of
2 CONC  Turenne to him in 1350 for 145,000 gold florins[1657]: “Dominus Iohannes comes Insulæ...filius et heres quondam domini Bernardi comitis Insulæ” certified that “Guillelmus Rogerii de Belloforti filius emancipatus...domini Guillerm
2 CONC i Rogerii comitis Bellifortis et vicecomitis Motæ” agreed to buy “vicecomitatum Turenæ” from “domina Cecilia de Convenis comitissa Urgelli et vicecomitissa Ageris et Turenæ heredeque...domini Bernardi bonæ memoriæ comitis Convenar
2 CONC um et vicecomitis Turenæ patris sui defuncti”, naming her sisters Jeanne and Eléonore, by charter dated 25 Feb 1350 (O.S.?)[1658].  “Domino Guillelmo comite Bellifortis vicecomiteque Motæ” granted “comitatum...Bellifortis” to “Rog
2 CONC erio eius filio emancipato”, and if he died childless to “dominos Guillelmum vicecomitem Turenæ et Marquesium filios dicti domini comitis donatoris”, and providing for “domino Hugone Tutellensi et P. Bellifortis cardinalibus...Nic
2 CONC olaum de Belloforti filium dicti domini comitis”, by charter dated 26 Mar 1360[1659].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (17 Nov 1349) ELEONORE de Comminges, daughter of BERNARD [VIII] Comte de Comminges & his third wife Mathe de l'Isle-Jourdain (-1397).  The testament of “Bernhardus...comes Convenarum, vicecomeque Turenæ”, dated 26 Mar 1335
2 CONC , provided dowries for “dominæ Iohannæ filiæ suæ...dominæ Hellionordi filiæ suæ”[1660].  The testament of “domina Matha de Insula comitissa Convenarum”, dated 1352, bequeathed property to “...dominæ Alienordi de Convenis vicecomit
2 CONC issæ Turenæ filiæ suæ...filiabus Ioannæ et Alienordi et cæteris liberis ipsius dominæ Alienordis vicecomitissæ predictæ...”[1661].
2 CONT
2 CONT   Guillaume [III] & his wife had five children: 
