1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matilde_d%27Altavilla_(contessa_di_Tolosa)_
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MATHILDE of Sicily'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From Medlands:
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SICILY.htm#Mathildediedbefore1094<br/>
2 CONT 2.         MATHILDE of Sicily (1062-before 1094).  Malaterra records the marriage of "Raimundus comes Provinciarum" and "Matildem filiam suam [Rogerii Siculorum comitis]…de prima uxore" which he dates to 1080[411].  The primary so
2 CONC urce which confirms her first marriage has not yet been identified.  According to Houben[412], Mathilde who married Robert Comte d'Eu was the daughter of Roger I Count of Sicily by his second wife, and a different person from Math
2 CONC ilde wife of Raymond Comte de Saint-Gilles.  No source is quoted, but this seems unlikely from a chronological point of view as Roger's second marriage took place in [1077], and Robert Comte d'Eu died in [1089/93].  In addition, i
2 CONC t seems unlikely that Roger, at the height of his power as count of Sicily in the late 1080s, would have agreed to his daughter's marriage to an obscure count in northern France while he was arranging royal marriages for his other
2 CONC  daughters.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (repudiated before [1080][413]) as his second wife, ROBERT Comte d'Eu, son of GUILLAUME Comte d'Hiémois et d'Eu [Normandie] & his wife Lesceline de Tourville (-8 Sep [1089/93], bur Le Tréport).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1080, divorced [1088]) as his third wife, RAYMOND de Toulouse, son of PONS Comte de Toulouse & his third wife Almodis de La Marche (-castle of Mount Pèlerin near Tripoli, Palestine 28 Feb 1105).  He succeeded his
2 CONC  brother in 1094 as RAYMOND IV Comte de Toulouse.  
