1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Almodis of Toulouse''' (d. after 1132), married Pierre I, Comte de Melgueil (d. after 27 Apr 1085), in 1065 (Cawley, 2006).
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Pons Guillaume de Toulouse (d 1060) & his wife Almodis de la Marche (d 1071), whom he repudiated before 1053.  The elder Almodis married a 3rd time to Raimund Berenguer, conde de Barcelona (d 1076).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierre_Ier_de_Melgueil
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Almodis de Toulouse''' (av. 1053-ap. 1132), fille de Pons, comte de Toulouse et d'Almodis de la Marche de qui il aura mariée en 1066 à Pierre Ier (♰ v. 1086), comte de Melgueil[37].  Il est le fils de Raymond Ier de Melgueil et
2 CONC  de Béatrice du Poitou. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariage et succession
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre de Melgueil épousa Almodis de Toulouse, fille de Pons, comte de Toulouse et d'Almodis de la Marche de qui il aura[HL Tome III 2],[1] :
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Raymond II, qui lui succéda dans le comté de Melgueil ;
2 CONT #     Pons, qui devint abbé de Cluny (1109-1122) ;
2 CONT #     Ermessende, mariée à Guilhem V de Montpellier ;
2 CONT #     Adèle, mariée à Pierre Raymond du Puy (1070-1110), frère d'Amiel Raymond du Puy, évêque de Toulouse (1105-1139) et parent de Raymond du Puy, second supérieur de l'ordre de l'Hôpital (1123-1158/60)[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE.htm#AlmodisMPierreMelgueil
2 CONT
2 CONT PONS GUILLAUME de Toulouse, son of GUILLAUME III "Taillefer" Comte de Toulouse & his second wife Emma de Provence ([995/97]-1060, bur Toulouse, Saint-Sernin) ... m secondly ([1045] repudiated 1053 after 29 Jun) as her second husba
2 CONC nd, ALMODIS de la Marche, repudiated wife of HUGUES V "le Pieux" Seigneur de Lusignan, daughter of BERNARD I Comte de la Marche & his wife Amelia - (-murdered 1071). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Pons & his second wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 '''ALMODIS de Toulouse''' (-[after 1132]).  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  "Petrus comes…filius Raymundo comite, genetrice…mea Beatrice" donated property to the church of Maguelonne
2 CONC  by charter dated 23 Jul 1079, signed by "uxore sua Adalmudis"[432].  "Petrus Substantionis comes filius Beatricis et uxor mea Almodis" donated property to the church of Maguelonne by charter dated Jan 1083[433].  "Petrus…comes Me
2 CONC lguoriensis…cum uxore mea Almodis et filiis meis" donated property to the monastery of Saint-Pons de Thomières by charter dated 26 Feb 1083[434].  "Petrus comes Melgoriensis" donated "comitatum Substantionem Quam episcopatum Magal
2 CONC onensem" to Pope Gregory VII, who regranted him the counties for life, by charter dated 27 Apr 1085, subscribed by "Adalmodis comitissa, Raymundus comes filius eius"[435].  The testament of “Bernardus comes Melgorii” dated 1132 wa
2 CONC s made in the presence of “…comitissa avia mea…”[436], although this could possibly refer to the testator´s maternal grandmother who has not otherwise been identified.  m ([1065]) PIERRE Comte de Melgueil, son of RAYMOND [I] Comte
2 CONC  de Melgueil & his wife Beatrix [de Poitou] (-after 1085). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc255726469 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Raymond [I] & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         PIERRE de Melgueil (-after 27 Apr 1085).  Comte de Melgueil. .... m ([1065]) '''ALMODIS de Toulouse''', daughter of PONS Comte de Toulouse & his second wife Almodis de la Marche (-after 1132). .. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre & his wife had four children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''RAYMOND de Melgueil''' (-[1120]).  m MARIE, daughter of -
2 CONT * b)         '''PONS de Melgueil''' (-Sept-Salles 28 Dec 1125, bur Saint-André).    The Chronicle of Saint-Maxence records the succession in 1109 of "Pontius filius comitis Mirguliæ" as abbot of Cluny[509].
2 CONT * c)         '''-- de Melgueil''' (-after 5 Jun 1156). [m] (Betrothed [1080]) GUILLAUME [V] Seigneur de Montpellier, son of GUILLAUME [IV] Seigneur de Montpellier & his wife Ermengarde - (-before 21 Feb 1122).  
2 CONT * d)         '''ADELA de Melgueil''' .  "Raimundus comes Melgoriensis" made his testament "ire volens in Jerusalem" dated to [1110], naming "soror mea Adala", and referring to but not naming his wife and his son[516].  
2 CONT * 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Almodis (Toulouse) de Mortain (1045-1132)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Toulouse-121 : accessed 18 April 2025).
