2 CONT 5.         BEATRICE (-after 1268).  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Neocastro records that "comes…Galvanus Beatricem filiam suam" married "Conradus de Antiochia"[869].  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the Istoria 
2 CONC of Saba Malaspina which names "Galvanus Lancea comes Principatus et Fundorum, marescallus regni" as "socer" of "Corrado de Antiochia comes Alba, regis eiusdem nepos"[870]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' [m''' firstly UGOLINO di Serro .''']'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [secondly] (1258 before 8 Jul) CORRADO d'Antiochia Conte di Loretto, son of FEDERIGO di Antiochia, Vicar General of the March of Ancona and Duchy of Spoleto [Hohenstaufen] & his wife Margherita di Poli (-after 1301).  Cont
2 CONC e di Alba, Celano, Laureto ed Abruzzo 1267. 
2 CONT
