2 CONT i)          '''FEDERIGO''' (-Palermo 22 Jul 1305).  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Neocastro names "Fridericus, Henricus et Galvanus" as the children of "Conradus de Antiochia" and his wife[753].  An epigraph records the dea
2 CONC th 22 Jul 1305 of "Dominus Fridericus miles…domini Conradi di Antiochia comitis filius et reverendi patris Bartholomæi Archiep. Parnorm. frater"[754].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   m ---.  The name of Federigo´s wife is not known.  Federigo & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT *(a)        CORRADO (-after [1320]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   
2 CONT
