1 NAME Guido /Embriaco/
2 GIVN Guido
2 SURN Embriaco
2 _MARNM Embriaco
1 NAME Guido II Embriaco, signore di Gibelletto
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE FEB 1282
1 OCCU Lord of Giblet
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_II_Embriaco
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TRIPOLI.htm#GuyEmbriacodied1282
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         '''GUY [II] '''(-murdered Nephin Jan 1282).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Balon, Gui, Johan, Bauduin et Maire" as the children of "Henri…seignor de Giblet" & his wife[341].  He succeeded his father as Lord o
2 CONC f Jebail.  He adopted the name and arms of Ibelin[342].  In 1277, he kidnapped the heiress of the Aleman family to marry her to his brother, triggering a quarrel with Bohémond VII Count of Tripoli who had intended her to marry the
2 CONC  nephew of Bartholomew Bishop of Tortosa, and afterwards fled to the Templars.  He defeated Count Bohémond, who had set out to attack Jebail, north of Botrun[343].  Guy defeated Count Bohémond once more in 1278, but the latter too
2 CONC k his revenge in Jan 1282 when he captured Guy and his brothers in Tripoli and buried them up to their necks in a ditch and left them to starve to death[344].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MARGUERITE of Sidon, daughter of JULIEN Garnier Lord of Sidon & his wife Euphemie of Armenia.  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Balian, Johan et Marguerite" as the three children of "Julien…sire de Saiete" and his wife "Femie
2 CONC , la fille au roi Heiton d'Ermenie", stating that Marguerite married "Gui le seignor de Giblet"[345].  The retrospective dispensation issued by Pope Nicholas IV for the marriage of "Guido de Ibelino, dominus Gibeleti, quondam" and
2 CONC  "Margarita quondam" is dated 23 May 1289[346].  Guy & his wife had four children (who were legitimated per dispensationem post matrimonium contractum 23 May 1289, on the basis that their parents' marriage had been contracted with
2 CONC out the necessary Papal dispensation, being related in the 4o degree[347]):
