2 CONT iii)        PIERRE (-1310 or after).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Piere, Sauve, Marie et Kateline" as the four children of "Gui…sire de Giblet" & his wife, stating that Pierre "morut"[357].  He succeeded his father in
2 CONC  1282 as titular Lord of Jebail, but the town was occupied by Bohémond VII Count of Tripoli and captured by the Egyptians in 1289[358].  Pope Nicholas IV instructed "Bybliensi et Sidoniensi episcopis" to legitimate "Petrum, Silves
2 CONC trum, Catherinam et Mariam…filios quondam Guidonis de Ybelino domini Gibeleti et quondam Margarethæ uxoris eius", who had married without dispensation despite 4o consanguinity, by charter dated 17 Apr 1289[359].  His possession of
2 CONC  Jebail was confirmed by the Sultan in 1289, but he lost the territory in [1300] and left Palestine for Cyprus[360].  Bailli of Cyprus 1308/1310.  [361]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [firstly] as her second husband, DOUCE de Gaurelée, widow of JEAN de Piquigny, daughter of ---.  [362]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [secondly] AGNES Embriaco, widow of GAUVAIN de la Roche, daughter of BARTHELEMY Embriaco & his wife ---. 
