2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00093466&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Guido von Ibelin (franz: Guy d'Ibelin; † nach Mai 1255) aus dem Haus Ibelin war Marschall, später Konstabler des Königreichs Zypern. Er war ein jüngerer Sohn des Johann von Ibelin, des „alten Herrn von Beirut“, und der Melisende v
2 CONC on Arsuf. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Ehe und Nachkommen[Bearbeiten | Quelltext bearbeiten] Guido war verheiratet mit Philippine Barlais, der Tochter des Amalrich Barlais, Herr von Blanchegarde, ihre Kinder waren:
2 CONT # Balduin († nach 1286), Connétable von Zypern, Bailli von Jerusalem;
2 CONT # Johann († ermordet 1276);
2 CONT # Aimerich;
2 CONT # Balian (* 1240, † 1302), Seneschall von Zypern 1286–1301;
2 CONT # Philipp (* 1253, † 1318), Seneschall von Zypern 1301–1318;
2 CONT # Isabella (* 1241, † 1324), ∞ König Hugo III. von Zypern;
2 CONT # Alix (* 1255) ∞ Eudes de Dampierre-sur-Salon († vor 1291);
2 CONT # Eschiva, Nonne;
2 CONT # Melisende († jung);
2 CONT # Maria († jung).
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CYPRUS.htm#GuyIbelindied1255B
2 CONT
2 CONT GUY Ibelin, son of JEAN Ibelin Lord of Beirut & his second wife Mélisende of Arsur ([1215/18]-after May 1255).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Bellian seignor de Baruth, et Baudoyn le Seneschau, et Hue le Fort, et Ysabia
2 CONC u qui fu nonain, et Johan de Ybelin…seignor d'Arsur, et Gui le conestable de Chypre" as the children of "Johan…de Ybelin…seignor de Baruth" and his wife Melisende[722].  The Chronicle of Philippe de Novare names "messier Bauduyn e
2 CONC t messier Hue et messier Guy" as the three sons of "monseignor de Baruth"[723].  He fought at the battle of Agridi in 1232, being of age at the time.  Marshal of Cyprus [1248].  Constable of Cyprus [1250].  He was taken prisoner a
2 CONC t the battle of Mansurah in 1250[724]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1240]) PHILIPPA Barlais, daughter of AIMERY Barlais & his wife Agnès de Marqab.  The Lignages d'Outremer refers to the wife of "Gui de Ybelin, conestable de Chypre, mere de ces enfanz" as a daughter of "Haymeri Barlais" 
2 CONC and his wife Agnes, daughter of "Bertran seignor dou Marguat" and his wife Raymonde of Beirut[725].  Another manuscript of the Lignages d'Outremer clarifies that she was "Phelippe, la fille Heimeri Barlais"[726]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy & his wife had ten children:
