2 CONT 1.         IOANNES [I] .  The name of Theodora´s husband is known only from the Memorial of their son "Crescentius…Iohanne patre Theodora matre" states that he died "VII Jul 984"[766].  It is not known whether he was Theodora´s on
2 CONC ly husband, or that he was also the father of her daughters Marozia [II], Stefania [I].  However, the fact that his great-granddaughter Rogata, descended from his son Crescentius, named her daughter Marozia suggests that the coupl
2 CONC e may have been the parents of all the children who are shown below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' THEODORA, daughter of TEOFILACTO [I] & his wife Theodora --- (-950).  Liudprand names "Marotiam et Theodora" as the two daughters of Theodora[767].  Her parentage and the names of her two daughters are confirmed by a chart
2 CONC er dated 14 Jan 945, reproduced in a notarial transcript dated 1301, which records a donation to the monastery of SS Andrea e Gregorio "Clivuscauri" and names "Albericus…princeps atque omnium Romanorum senator atque Sergius…episco
2 CONC pus sancte Nepesine ecclesie, nec non et Constantinus illustris vir atque Bertha nobilissima puella uterine, et germani fratres Marozze quondam Romanorum senatricis filii, nec non et Marozza seu Stephania nobilissima femina, germa
2 CONC ne sorores et consobrine eorum Theodore quondam Romanorum senatricis filie", subscribed by (in order) "Alberic, Marozza, Stephania, Bertha, Sergius, Constantine"[768].  
2 CONT
