2 CONT c)         [THEODORA (-before 963).  Senatrix.  No primary source has been found which confirms that Theodora, wife of Ioannes III Duke of Naples, was the sister of Marozia [II] and Stefania [I].  However, the title senatrix attri
2 CONC buted to her, as well as her name, suggests that this affiliation may be correct.  The dating clause of a charter dated to [945/60] refers to "principatum ducatus totius Campaniæ dominantibus Iohanne et Marino…ducibus et consulibu
2 CONC s" and "[Iohannis] coniugem…Theodoram…senatricem Romanorum"[776].  The Memorial of her son "Landolfus…senatricis Theodoræ…Ioha[nnis] consulis atque ducis…progenies" states that he was "adoptivum Maroza senatrix"[777], which sugges
2 CONC ts a close family relationship with Marozia.  "Iohannes…consul et dux filius…domini Marini duci" exchanged property with "Cesario ferrario filio Iohannis dudum ferrarii et maiorarii postmodum…monachi", with the consent of "Theodor
2 CONC e…ducisse coniugi meæ", by charter dated 3 Nov [951][778].  
2 CONT
