2 CONT '''LANDOLF''', son of LANDOLF III joint Prince of Capua & his wife Gemma of Naples (-961).  According to the "Catalogus Principum Capuæ", "Atenulfus III et Landulfus II, filii Landulfi" ruled jointly with their father[1575].  "Lan
2 CONC dulph Rufus filius Landulph Antipatru, germano Athnulph de Calinulu" succeeded his brother in 943 as LANDOLF IV Prince of Capua and Benevento[1576].  According to the Annales Beneventani, "Landolfi filii eius [=Landolfus princeps]
2 CONC " ceased to be Prince of Benevento in 944 "in the fourth year of his reign", when his son Pandolf was installed as prince[1577].  The Chronicon Vulturnense records a charter dated Aug 945 "sexto anno principatus domni Landulfi…pri
2 CONC ncipis et anno secundo domni Pandulfi eius filii"[1578].  "Landolfus princeps…periit inter Agarenis"[1579].  The Chronicon Vulturnense records "Landolfus et Pandolfus filius eiusdem…Langobardorum gentis" confirmed the grant of fis
2 CONC hery rights "in lacum Patrensem" to the monastery of Volturno, granted by "domna Gemma principissa…genitrice nostra", by charter dated 960[1580].  The dating clause of a charter dated May 961, under which "Andreas filius Loperissi
2 CONC " donated property to Cava monastery, refers to the twenty-second year of "domni Landolfi…principis" and the eighteenth year of "principatus domni Paldolfi filii eius"[1581].  The Chonicon Monasterii Beneventani records the death 
2 CONC in 961 of "Landulphus Princeps" and the succession (in Benevento) of "Landulphus germanus Pandulphi Principis"[1582]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [935] ) ---. '' '''There are two possibilities for the wife''' '' of Prince Landolf IV.  
2 CONT Stasser suggests that she was''' ''MARIA di Gaeta'' ''', daughter of DOCIBILIS II Lord of Gaeta & his wife Orania of Naples[1583].  He highlights that "Maria principessa" is named as one of the daughters of Docibilis in his testam
2 CONC ent dated 954, and points out that, as all the wives of the contemporary princes of Salerno are known, she must have been the wife of one of the princes of Capua-Benevento.  
2 CONT A second possibility is that she was''' ''EUANTHIA'' ''', daughter of ---.  The Chronicon Comitum Capuæ names "Landulph et Yvantie ucsore sue" when referring to a donation[1584], which appears to refer to Prince Landolf IV.  Stass
2 CONC er points out that this source is a late, spurious compilation[1585].  No indication has been found of any earlier sources on which this forgery may have been based, but the name is presumably Byzantine as it recalls "Euanthia" wi
2 CONC fe of Grimoald III Prince of Benevento (who died in 806). 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Prince Landolf IV & his wife had [six] children: 
2 CONT * 1.         PANDOLF (-Mar 981).  The Annales Beneventani record that "Pandolfus filius eius [=Landolfus princeps]" was installed as Prince of Benevento in 944[1586].  The Chronicon Vulturnense records a charter dated Aug 945 "sex
2 CONC to anno principatus domni Landulfi…principis et anno secundo domni Pandulfi eius filii"[1587].  He succeeded his father in 961 as PANDOLF I "Capiferreus/Ironhead" Prince of Capua and Benevento. -        see below.  
2 CONT * 2.         IOANNES (-974).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Archbishop of Capua. 
2 CONT * 3.         LANDOLF (-968).  … The Annales Beneventani record the death of Landolf V in 968[1590].  m (Summer 958) GAITELGRIMA,
2 CONT * 4.         [SICHELGARDA .  Stasser proposes that the wife of Transmundo [I] was the daughter of Landulf IV Prince of Capua and Benevento[1603]. 
2 CONT * 5.         [GEMMA (-after Oct 1006).  Gemma, widow of Cadolo, is named in a charter dated Aug 982[1606].  Stasser suggests that Gemma, wife of Cadolo, was the daughter of Landulf IV Prince of Capua and Benevento[1607].  m ([953/
2 CONC 64]) as his second wife, CADOLO Conte [in Tuscany], son of CORRADO Conte & his wife Ermengarda --- (-before Aug 982).] 
2 CONT * 6.         WILLA (-after Oct 1007).  "Guillia filia bone memorie Landulfi et relicta bone memorie Rodolfi comes" donated property by charter dated Aug 988[1608].  "Guillia filia bone memorie Landulfi que fuit princeps Beneventan
2 CONC orum" donated property by charter dated Oct 1007[1609].  m RODOLFO [II] Aldobrandeschi, son of RODOLFO [I] Aldobrandeschi & his wife --- (-before 988). 
2 CONT
