2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Elizabeth Herbert:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10499.htm#i104988
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Herbert, Baroness Herbert [1]
2 CONT *F, #104988, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1476, 
2 CONT *d. between 29 January 1509 and 21 March 1513
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 Apr 2004
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Herbert, Baroness Herbert was born circa 1476.[1] She was the daughter of William Herbert, 2nd Earl of Pembroke and Mary Wydeville.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Charles Somerset, 1st Earl of Worcester, son of Henry Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset and Joan Hill, on 2 June 1492.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died between 29 January 1509 and 21 March 1513.[1] She was buried at St. George's Chapel, Windsor Castle, Windsor, Berkshire, England.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She succeeded to the title of 3rd Baroness Herbert [E., 1461] on 16 July 1491, suo jure.[1] From 2 June 1492, her married name became Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Elizabeth Herbert, Baroness Herbert and Charles Somerset, 1st Earl of Worcester
2 CONT *1. Henry Somerset, 2nd Earl of Worcester+[2] b. c 1496, d. 26 Nov 1549
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/2, page 848. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume XII/2, page 851.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Somerset, Countess of Worcester and 3rd Baroness Herbert (c.1476 – c.1513) was the daughter of William Herbert, 2nd Earl of Pembroke and his first wife, Mary Woodville.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Charles Somerset, 1st Earl of Worcester on June 2, 1492. Their only son was Henry Somerset, 2nd Earl of Worcester.
2 CONT
2 CONT As her father had no sons, Elizabeth succeeded to the barony in 1491, but could not succeed to the earldom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died some time between January 29, 1509 and March 21, 1513, and was buried in St George's Chapel, Windsor Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://welshjournals.llgc.org.uk/browse/viewpage/llgc-id:1277425/llgc-id:1288291/llgc-id:1288332/getText National Library of Wales journal  -  Cyf. 25, rh. 4 Gaeaf 1988 The marriages of knighted Welsh landowners, 1485-1558] 
2 CONC page 395
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Sir Charles Somerset (d. 1526) of Chepstow and Raglan and Kew, co. Surrey, raised to
2 CONT the peerage as Lord Herbert in 1503 or 1504 and created earl of Worcester in 1514, m. (1) Elizabeth (W), d. of William Herbert (d. 1490), earl of Pembroke and Lord of Chepstow, Raglan and Gower; (2) Elizabeth (E), d. of Thomas Wes
2 CONC t (d. 1525), Lord De La Warr of co. Sussex; and (3) Eleanor (E), d. of Edward Sutton (d. 1532), lord Dudley, who after Somerset's death m., as his second wife, Leonard (d. 1541), Lord Grey (GEC, Complete Peerage, vol. xii, pt. ii,
2 CONC  p. 850).
