1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ID: I32467 View Post-em! Name: Anthony GREY , of Ruthin, Sir 1 Sex: M Birth: ABT 1450 in Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales Death: BEF 26 JUN 1480 in (dsp & vp) 1 Burial: St. Albans Abbey, Hertfordshire, England Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     ANTHONY GREY, 1st son and heir apparent. He was knighted in the Tower on the eve of the Queen's Coronation, Ascension Day, 1465. As Anthony Grey of Ruthyn, knight. he was named in a commission of array with his father in Bucks
2 CONC , Beds, co. Cambridge and Northants, 29 October 1469 and 14 February 1469/70, and was on similar commissions 11 May 1471 and 7 March 1471/2. He was a justice of the Peace in Beds 1469-76 and in 1479, and in Northants 1469-1476/7, 
2 CONC and 1477 and May 1480. On 3 June 1470 he had a grant of 100 marks yearly from the customs in Devon and Cornwall. On 3 July 1471 he was present in the Parliament Chamber at Westminster and swore to accept Edward, Prince of Wales as
2 CONC  heir to the Crown. As Antony Grey knight, lord of Gray Ruthin, the King's kinsman, he had a grant of Wrestlingworth and other manors 28 April 1474. On 8 May 1475 he was about to go across the seas. On 13 August 1475 he was a witn
2 CONC ess of the treaty between Edward IV and Louis XI near Péronne.
2 CONT
2 CONT     He married Joan, sister of Elizabeth, the Queen consort, daughter, and [in her issue] coheir of Richard [Widevill] 1st EARL RIVERS, by Jacqueline or Jacquette, DUCHESS OF BEDFORD, daughter of Pierre DE LUXEMBOURG, COUNT OF SAI
2 CONC NT POL, CONVERSANO and BRIENNE. He died s.p. and v.p. between 15 May and 26 June 1480, and was buried in the Abbey of St. Albans: brass. [Complete Peerage VII:165-6, XIV:408, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Edmund 4th Baron GREY , 1st Earl of Kent, Sir b: 26 OCT 1416 in Ruthin, Denbighshire, Wales Mother: Katherine PERCY b: 28 MAY 1423 in Leckenfield, Beveryley, Yorkshire East Riding, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Joan WYDEVILLE b: ABT 1449 in Grafton Regis, Northamptonshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Title: Complete Peerage of England Scotland Ireland Great Britain and the United Kingdom, by G. E Cokayne, Sutton Publishing Ltd, 2000
2 CONT     Page: VII:165-6 
