0 @N6000000002322288565@ NOTE Elizabeth was a commoner, a woman of great beauty, but already a widow with
1 CONT two sons when she married Edward. As a daughter of the Lancastrians, the
1 CONT traditional enemies of the Yorkists, and because she was not of royal rank,
1 CONT the mariage was repugnant to the ruling nobility of the house of York. Why
1 CONT Elizabeth, who had taken sanctuary, surrendered her young son and and
1 CONT daughters to Richard III is not clear. Soon, both young sons disappeared from
1 CONT Richard's custody, presumably murdered.
