1 CONC he legitimate heir, his young nephew,reached majority in 1157, as Ramon Berenguer III of Provence. Whenthis count of Provence died in 1166 without a male heir, he wassucceeded by Ramon Berenguer IV's son Alfonso II, king of Aragon
1 CONC . Byhis wars and conquests from the Moors--Tortosa (1148), Lerida,Mequinenza, and Fraga (1149), and Prades and Siurana (1153)--RamonBerenguer IV definitively established the boundaries of theprincipality of Catalonia. [Encyclopaed
