0 @N6000000002322305224@ NOTE Joan defended her claim as well as that of the house of Anjou to the throne
1 CONT of Naples, only to lose it to Charles of Durazzo (Charles III of Naples).
1 CONT Beautiful and intelligent, she was also a patron of the poets and scholars of
1 CONT her time. Charles of Durazzo, whom childless Joan had previously recognized
1 CONT as her heir to the throne of Naples, then changing the heir to Louis, Duke
1 CONT d'Anjou, secured the aid of the pope and was crowned King of Naples in 1381.
1 CONT After recapturing Naples, Joan was imprisoned, where he had her suffocated.
