1 CONT Margaret of York (10 Apr 1472 - 11 Dec 1472) was a namesake niece of Margaret of York, Duchess of Burgundy. She was the fifth child and fourth daughter of Edward IV of England and Elizabeth Woodville.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was a younger sister of Elizabeth of York, Mary of York, Cecily of York and Edward V of England. She was also an older sister of Richard of Shrewsbury, 1st Duke of York, Anne of York, George Plantagenet, Duke of Bedford, Cathe
1 CONC rine of York and Bridget of York.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was born in Winchester Castle but died of natural causes eight months later. She was buried in Westminster Abbey.
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret's sarcophagus was originally placed to fit in the steps of the shrine of St. Edward the Confessor but but moved at the time of the disolution of the monasteries to the edge of the chapel. The step edging around the sides 
1 CONC can however still be seen.
1 CONT
1 CONT An annotated history of the history of the Abbey in the Abbey's library states that the lid was removed in more modern times and the sarcophagus found to be empty. The monumental brass originally on the top of Margaret's tomb is l
1 CONC ong since missing, but the originally wording around the edge and on the surface plaque was recorded historically.
1 CONT  This English biographical article is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
1 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_York_%281472%29"
1 CONT Categories: English people stubs | 1472 births | 1472 deaths | People from Winchester | House of
